{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' AGENTS.md; sed -n '1,240p' PROGRESS.md; sed -n '1,220p' CONTEXT-LEDGER.md; sed -n '1,220p' reviews/P50-normal-faithful-corner-trace-closeout-rerun.md; sed -n '1,220p' reviews/P47-center-finite-projection-core-closeout.md 2>/dev/null || true\"","aggregated_output":"# Manuscript-Only Context Policy\n\n## Source authority\n\nFor manuscript-facing statements, the sole mathematical source is\n`sources/manuscript/main.tex`.\nThe local summary and locator record is `SOURCE-CONTRACT.md`. Do not modify\nthe manuscript from this project.\n\nEvery claim described as coming from the manuscript must identify an exact\nline range in `main.tex`. Repository history, earlier chat context, and other\nartifacts are not substitute sources.\n\n## Context firewall\n\nDo not introduce, assume, or attribute to the manuscript any gLU,\nrefinement, layer-coherence, or finite-coordinate construction unless it is\npresent in the cited manuscript lines or is explicitly introduced as a new\nauxiliary assumption. A Lean file compiling does not make its unstated\nphysical or operator-algebraic hypotheses part of the manuscript.\n\nClassify each item as one of:\n\n1. **manuscript-derived**: exact source locator and no stronger conclusion;\n2. **auxiliary assumption**: explicitly labelled and used only conditionally;\n3. **Lean infrastructure**: reusable formal mathematics that makes no source\n   claim; or\n4. **legacy exploratory work**: retained for reference but unavailable as\n   support for a manuscript-derived assertion.\n\n`CONTEXT-LEDGER.md` records the current legacy items.\n\n## Current formalization boundary\n\nThe target discussed in the manuscript is the short-range regional-algebra\nstatement at `main.tex:1740-1752`; its proposed proof is at\n`main.tex:1891-2004`. Keep separate the asserted algebraic identification,\nthe product-state/GNS steps, the unformalized operator-algebraic completion and\nspatial tensor-product steps, and the trace conclusion. A tracial state is\nappropriate only for the finite pure-sector case. The infinite pure-sector\ntarget instead calls for a faithful normal semifinite trace/weight when the\nrequired hypotheses and von Neumann infrastructure are supplied.\n\n## Aristotle task packets\n\nEvery new task under `aristotle_tasks/` must begin with exactly one context\ndeclaration:\n\n- `Source basis: main.tex:<line range>` for a manuscript-facing task; or\n- `Infrastructure only:` for reusable Lean material that makes no manuscript\n  claim.\n\nIt must then list every auxiliary assumption, state its exact Lean target, and\nsay whether its conclusion is conditional. A task may not cite a legacy\nartifact as its source basis. Use `aristotle_tasks/TEMPLATE.md` for new\npackets.\n\n## Active two-lane plan execution\n\nThe active Codex/Aristotle execution plan is `PLAN.md`, with the approval\nrecord in `work/TWO-LANE-FORMALIZATION-DECISION.md`. Before starting any new\npackage in the P47--P61 program, read both files and the closeout/audit record\nfor every declared predecessor.\n\nEvery future packet must include a `Plan alignment` section containing:\n\n1. the exact package identifier and its lane: `G` (general finite-corner and\n   central type-III exclusion), `H` (explicit local-hyperbolic tensor-factor\n   model), `shared`, or `reconnection`;\n2. the predecessor packages that have already been integrated, or `none` for\n   a foundation package;\n3. the exact gate this package is permitted to discharge; and\n4. downstream claims it is forbidden to make.\n\nThe Aristotle prompt must explicitly instruct the worker to read the active\nplan and respect this section. A package may use only integrated, compiled\npredecessors; a finished remote job is not a dependency until it has passed\nthe local semantic audit. Do not infer a theorem from a later package, and do\nnot submit a dependent packet before its listed prerequisites are integrated.\n\nFor Lane G, the required conclusion is a nonzero finite **projection** in\nevery nonzero central summand; a finite-dimensional subalgebra is not enough.\nFor Lane H, do not call the local algebra a factor until the spatial tensor\nfactorization and factorhood of both factors are proved. Neither lane may\nclaim a global trace/weight unless it constructs or explicitly assumes one.\n\n## Verification and reporting\n\nReport Lean compilation separately from mathematical validation. For each\nmanuscript-facing milestone, state which source clauses are represented, which\nassumptions remain external, and which analytic/von Neumann-algebraic claims\nare not yet formalized in the pinned Mathlib version.\n# Formalization progress\n\n## Context policy (2026-08-05)\n\nAll future manuscript-facing formalization takes its context only from\n`SOURCE-CONTRACT.md`, with exact locators in the manuscript `main.tex`. Earlier\ngLU/refinement/layer-coherence artifacts remain available only as explicitly\nlabelled legacy infrastructure; they are not manuscript hypotheses. See\n`AGENTS.md` and `CONTEXT-LEDGER.md`.\n\nThe manuscript-facing module sequence is now `Formalization.Manuscript`:\nsource boundary, finite model, algebraic limit, product state, conditional GNS\nbridge, trace dichotomy, and only then the pending theorem contract. Existing\nimplementation files remain in place and are imported through facades.\n\n- P17 — under a supplied finite adapted-coordinate/word realization, the\n  finite pure/mixed product state is exactly the stabilizer indicator on every\n  supplied source Pauli basis word.\n- P18 — a supplied finite matrix-factor tensor decomposition transports the\n  finite product trace to an algebraic tracial state with its elementary-tensor\n  formula.\n- P19 — a supplied C-star model plus compatible states packages the existing\n  GNS unitary and algebraic commutant transport into one bridge interface.\n- P23 — supplied coherent finite-stage star equivalences induce the infinite\n  algebraic direct-limit regional equivalence `alpha`, with finite-stage and\n  inverse formulas. No C-star or von Neumann extension is claimed.\n- P24 — compatible target-stage algebraic states pull back along `alpha` to a\n  unique algebraic direct-limit state with its exact finite-stage expectation\n  formula and conditional stabilizer-indicator corollary.\n- P25 — supplied C-star completions and an extension of `alpha` yield an\n  isometric continuous C-star equivalence and continuous state pullback;\n  existence of those completions remains an explicit assumption.\n\n## Checked Lean results\n\n- `TPT-001` / `TPT-002` — an algebraic tracial state pulls back along a\n  complex `StarAlgEquiv`.\n- TPT-003 — algebraic traciality is reflected as well as preserved by a\n  complex star-algebra equivalence; hence a nontracial product state cannot\n  become tracial after an algebraic coordinate identification.\n- `FMT-001` — the normalized trace on a nonempty finite full matrix algebra is\n  an algebraic tracial state.  Positivity is proved by the explicit\n  trace-of-a-star-square sum-of-squares identity.\n- `FSC-001` — a finite corner equipped with a star isomorphism to a full matrix\n  algebra inherits that algebraic tracial state.\n- `FTT-001` — the finite algebraic tensor product of two matrix factors is\n  identified by the Kronecker star isomorphism, and its normalized trace\n  factorizes on elementary tensors; tensoring with a matrix identity preserves\n  the trace.\n- `FAM-001` — if `R` has an algebraic tracial state, then its finite matrix\n  amplification `Matrix n n R` has the normalized diagonal tracial state.\n  Positivity is checked as a finite sum of coefficient-algebra star-squares.\n  An explicit `StarAlgEquiv` transports this finite type-I product trace to a\n  target algebra.\n- `TMT-001` — the finite type-I product is now identified canonically, not\n  supplied as an assumption: `Matrix n n ℂ ⊗[ℂ] R` is star-isomorphic to\n  `Matrix n n R`.  Its trace factors on elementary tensors as the normalized\n  matrix trace times the coefficient trace.\n- `DTT-001` — the actual dyadic finite-stage system is constructed as\n  `A₀ = ℂ`, `Aₙ₊₁ = Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) Aₙ`, with diagonal identity-qubit\n  embeddings.  Its normalized traces are compatible with every stage map,\n  and their algebraic directed limit carries the induced algebraic tracial\n  state.\n- FPU-001 — for every nonempty finite matrix factor, its algebraic tensor\n  product with the concrete dyadic algebraic limit carries the checked product\n  tracial state.  The theorem includes the elementary-tensor formula\n  tr_p(a) times qubitUHFTrace(u).\n- FPU-002 — any supplied regional `StarAlgEquiv` into that finite-pure\n  product model induces an algebraic tracial state on the regional algebra,\n  with the checked formula on inverse images of elementary tensors.\n- `AIT-001` — compatible unital cyclic finite-stage functionals glue to a\n  unital cyclic linear functional on mathlib's algebraic directed direct\n  limit.\n- `AIT-002` — compatible stagewise star-algebra maps induce an involutive,\n  additive, multiplication-reversing star on that algebraic direct limit.\n  Compatible algebraic tracial states then glue to an ordinary algebraic\n  tracial state there.\n- `SPC-001` — an adapted Hamel basis identifies the label space with finitely\n  supported X/Z coordinate labels and maps the singleton coordinate labels to\n  the chosen basis vectors.\n- ASC-001 — for a selected set of Z coordinates, Lean now identifies the\n  corresponding coordinate subspace both as the span of those Z basis\n  vectors and as the finite words with no X coordinate and no Z coordinate\n  outside the selected set.  This is the exact linear selection criterion\n  required before comparing the regional stabilizer state with the\n  pure/mixed product state.\n- FQS-001 — Lean now reads the recursive finite-qubit Pauli label as its\n  finite X/Z coordinate list and proves that the pure/mixed product-state\n  indicator is exactly the selected-Z condition: a pure coordinate has no X\n  exponent, and a mixed coordinate is the identity label.  Under an arbitrary\n  supplied adapted coordinate basis, that condition is literal membership in\n  the selected-Z stabilizer submodule.  The coherent direct-limit state theorem\n  has a corresponding selected-Z indicator form on source basis words.\n- `PCC-001` — a phase-corrected additive map of Pauli labels respects word\n  multiplication and star exactly when it satisfies explicit multiplier and\n  involution equations.  This isolates the cocycle data that symplecticity\n  alone does not supply.  The cross-algebra word-basis extension is now also\n  checked: its two compatibility equations and a specified Pauli-word basis\n  yield a genuine `StarAlgEquiv`.\n- `SCC-001` — the quotient of two multiplier phases is an additive character,\n  calibrating by an additive character preserves the multiplier equation, and\n  every additive character on a vector subspace extends to the ambient vector\n  space along a complementary subspace.  This is the exact algebraic\n  stabilizer-sign calibration: the finite-field character is self-conjugate,\n  and calibration preserves both Pauli-word compatibility equations.  The\n  concrete finite-support quadratic phase is now independently formalized;\n  relating it to the actual regional stabilizer convention remains separate.\n- QPR-001 — the explicit ZMod 4 finite-support quadratic refinement has its\n  polarization and diagonal identities fully checked.  Its discrepancy pairing\n  is additive in both words, symmetric for a symmetric discrepancy, and has\n  additive order two.  These facts instantiate the cross-algebra Pauli-word\n  multiplication and involution certificates and, with a supplied word-basis\n  linear equivalence, a `StarAlgEquiv`.\n- QPT-001 — the concrete finite-support phase theorem now composes that\n  `StarAlgEquiv` with the finite-pure times qubit-UHF trace transport: whenever\n  the regional Pauli-word exponents, involution phases, and word-basis map are\n  supplied, Lean constructs both the star-algebra equivalence and its induced\n  algebraic tracial state with the elementary-tensor product formula.  The\n  Pauli-word interface has been weakened from `Ring` to `Semiring`, the exact\n  structure carried by the concrete algebraic UHF direct limit.\n- PTO-001 — two isometries whose range projections sum to the identity rule\n  out even an algebraic unital cyclic trace.  This is the checked obstruction\n  behind the infinite-pure-sector case; the tracial-state theorem is therefore\n  deliberately limited to a finite pure matrix factor.\n- ALT-001 — compatible finite-stage `StarAlgEquiv`s and compatible target\n  algebraic tracial states induce a source-side algebraic tracial state on the\n  corresponding quasi-local direct limit.  The theorem evaluates it exactly\n  on every finite-stage representative.  The concrete finite-pure UHF trace\n  now has the matching finite-stage elementary-tensor formula.\n- FQP-001 — every finite stage of the dyadic qubit tower now has an explicit\n  ordered Pauli-word `StarSystem` and a complex Pauli-word basis.  The\n  identity-qubit embeddings preserve its words, basis vectors, multiplication\n  multipliers, and star multipliers under coherent label maps.  Thus the UHF\n  target-side finite-stage word hypotheses are no longer abstract assumptions;\n  assembling them into one global target word system remains open.\n- PMS-001 — for every Boolean sequence specifying whether each newly adjoined\n  qubit is pure or maximally mixed, the corresponding finite product\n  functionals are algebraic states, are compatible with all dyadic embeddings,\n  and induce an algebraic state on the UHF direct limit.  Their values on every\n  finite Pauli word are proved recursively: pure coordinates permit only zero\n  X exponent, while mixed coordinates permit only the identity word.  The\n  all-mixed specialization is proved equal to the previously checked UHF\n  tracial state.  Lean also proves that even the one-qubit pure specialization\n  is not cyclic and hence not an algebraic tracial state.\n- PTR-001 — this nontraciality is now proved at arbitrary finite and\n  direct-limit coordinates: if any Boolean coordinate is pure, explicit\n  matrix units witness a failure of cyclicity.  Consequently the algebraic\n  UHF product state is tracial if and only if every coordinate is maximally\n  mixed, in which case it is the checked UHF trace.\n- CBL-001 — finite-stage star-algebra equivalences need not be assumed\n  coherent on every algebra element: if the source connecting maps, target\n  vectors, and coordinate maps agree on a specified source basis, Lean proves\n  the full commuting square by linear-basis extensionality.\n- CPS-001 — a phase-corrected finite coordinate system now has a concrete\n  direct-limit state interface.  Coherent source basis transport, phases, and\n  finite Pauli labels imply full-stage equivalence coherence and hence a\n  star-algebra equivalence to the algebraic qubit-UHF direct limit; the induced\n  source state evaluates a basis word as its phase times the pure/mixed Pauli\n  selection indicator.  The all-mixed specialization pulls the UHF trace back\n  to a source algebraic tracial state; more generally its pure/mixed pullback\n  is tracial exactly when every coordinate is mixed.  Constructing the\n  regional inputs remains open.\n- ACS-001 — if supplied finite-stage regional data identify selected target\n  Z-coordinates with the actual source stabilizer words, Lean derives the\n  exact phase-calibrated stabilizer expectation formula on every source basis word.\n  The stronger form states that hypothesis as literal membership in the\n  selected-Z submodule of an adapted coordinate basis.  Thus the remaining\n  geometric work is isolated to constructing and coherently transporting that\n  coordinate data from a separately supplied finite-coordinate realization,\n  rather than to a hidden infinite-algebra assumption. The manuscript does not\n  presently supply that realization; see `SOURCE-CONTRACT.md`.\n- ALS-001 — compatible finite-stage star-algebra equivalences transport\n  compatible algebraic states (not only tracial states) to a quasi-local\n  algebraic direct limit.  This is the exact state-level interface required by\n  a coherent regional stabilizer-coordinate construction.\n- WBE-001 — if Pauli words form a complex linear basis, checking a\n  complex-linear map on every pair of basis words proves multiplicativity on\n  all finite sums.  The corresponding conjugate-linear basis argument proves\n  star preservation; a bijective unital map satisfying both checks is packaged\n  as a star-algebra equivalence.\n- ALC-001 — a compatible family of finite-stage star-algebra maps induces a\n  star-algebra map from the algebraic directed limit.  Compatible finite-stage\n  star-algebra equivalences induce a star-algebra equivalence of the two\n  algebraic limits.  The C-star norm extension remains open.\n- CSE-001 — once a source and target are supplied as complex C-star algebras,\n  Lean proves that every complex `StarAlgEquiv` is isometric and therefore\n  continuous with continuous inverse.  A continuous target functional pulls\n  back continuously along it.  This does not construct C-star norms or\n  completions for the algebraic direct-limit models.\n- CCF-001 — the pinned Mathlib supports the finite dyadic stages as genuine\n  C-star algebras and supports closure/minimality once an ambient C-star\n  algebra is supplied.  It does not provide the C-star inductive-limit\n  construction for the algebraic dyadic limit; this is recorded as an\n  explicit missing API rather than hidden behind an axiom.\n- NMC-001 — supplied finite C-star realizations of the coherent coordinate\n  maps are isometric and continuous, and the commuting inclusion squares\n  preserve the norm estimates.  The resulting dense-subalgebra estimate is\n  exactly the analytic input needed before extending the algebraic map to a\n  completion; no completion is constructed here.\n- BMC-001 — for a star subalgebra of bounded operators on a Hilbert space,\n  Lean now constructs the algebraic bicommutant as a concrete\n  `VonNeumannAlgebra`, with monotonicity, minimality, membership, and\n  idempotence lemmas.  The analytic strong/weak double-commutant theorem is\n  still explicitly absent from the pinned Mathlib and remains separate.\n- CCC-001 — from an explicitly supplied isometric star representation of a\n  pre-C-star algebra into bounded operators, Lean constructs the closed\n  operator-range C-star algebra, its isometric dense embedding, and the\n  uniqueness equivalence between two such concrete completions.  The faithful\n  operator representation of the project-specific algebraic limit is still a\n  separate obligation.\n\n## The exact theorem still to prove\n\nThe Overleaf short-range theorem asserts a regional von Neumann algebra\nisomorphism to a type-I factor tensor a hyperfinite type-II1 factor.  It is\nnot yet formalized as a theorem because the supplied manuscript proof leaves\nthe following essential premises open:\n\n1. a finite-support adapted symplectic coordinate map whose finite-stage\n   source bases, phase correction, and target Pauli labels are coherent along\n   an exhaustion;\n2. identification of the actual regional Pauli multiplier and involution\n   exponents with the finite-support coordinate discrepancy, followed by\n   calibration to the actual stabilizer character;\n3. the induced quasi-local C-star isomorphism;\n4. factorization of the regional state into pure and normalized-tracial\n   coordinate states; and\n5. a normal/spatial extension to the respective bicommutants.\n\nThe current pinned mathlib version includes preliminary abstract and concrete\nvon Neumann-algebra definitions, but lacks a finished API for infinite von\nNeumann tensor products, normal states/traces, hyperfiniteness, and factor\nclassification.  The project therefore does not introduce any axiom for the\ntarget theorem.\n\n## Last verification\n\n```text\nlake build\nlake build Formalization.AlgebraicLimitStateTransport Formalization.QubitMatrixState Formalization.FinitePureMixedQubitState Formalization\n# Context ledger\n\n## Legacy exploratory material: not manuscript authority\n\nThe following artifacts contain gLU, refinement, or layer-coherence language\nimported from broader repository history rather than from the manuscript named\nin `SOURCE-CONTRACT.md`:\n\n- `blueprints/002-aristotle-parallel-formalization.tex`;\n- `aristotle_tasks/P6-layered-direct-limit.md`;\n- `AristotleCandidates/LayeredDirectLimit.lean`;\n- `AristotleCandidates/RegionalWitness.lean`; and\n- `Formalization/CoherentPhaseQubitState.lean`.\n\nThey are preserved unchanged as useful exploratory or infrastructure work.\nThey may be cited only by a future task explicitly marked `Infrastructure\nonly`; they cannot establish a manuscript-derived hypothesis or conclusion.\n\n## Interpretation rule\n\nWhen an older document conflicts with `AGENTS.md` or `SOURCE-CONTRACT.md`, the\nnew manuscript-only policy governs all future task packets and reports. No\nhistorical label retroactively changes the source basis of a checked Lean\ntheorem.\n# P50 closeout rerun — normal faithful corner trace\n\n## Decision\n\n**Status: blocked; queue must halt.**\n\nThis rerun reviewed Aristotle task `292ec9c3-b24f-40ea-958e-835d0bae4379`\nafter its terminal `COMPLETE` status.  Its raw archive is already preserved as\n`aristotle_responses/P50-normal-faithful-corner-trace.tar.gz` (SHA-256\n`fd0d1163a25c0bce9299ee47729242662841def85d792242da1714dfd2839a31`) and\nits dependency-free quarantine extraction as\n`aristotle_responses/P50-quarantine/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p50-n98s99xk_aristotle/`.\nThe archive was not built, updated, or used for dependency fetching.  The only\npacket-authorized candidate is its\n`AristotleCandidates/NormalFaithfulCornerTrace.lean` (SHA-256\n`9b07496376b9a264645b9b1d8643e3710b0b9f3f85cc11a40109a1ffaaa713a9`).  It\nremains unintegrated.\n\nThe mandatory predecessor P49 is not locally accepted or integrated.  The\nauthoritative P49 closeout records `partial; queue must halt` because its\nsource locator omitted the finite-stage claims it used.  The untracked live\n`AristotleCandidates/FiniteCornerTrace.lean` is therefore not an integrated\npredecessor merely because it compiles.  P49C is integrated and locally\naudited, but it cannot substitute for P49.\n\nIndependently, the candidate fails P50's stated acceptance criterion: its\n`CornerData` has the load-bearing field\n`cstar_tracial : CornerTracialOn q Ω (A : Set (H →L[ℂ] H))`.  The exported\n`FaithfulCornerData.isFaithfulNormalTracialState` is consequently conditional\non supplied C-star cyclicity rather than deriving it by instantiating\n`CompatibleFiniteCodespaceSystem.finite_corner_trace`, as the packet requires.\nIts import of `FiniteCornerTrace` supplies the predicate name but does not\ndischarge this premise.  Thus the candidate silently weakens the requested\nroute even though its abstract conditional bridge type-checks.\n\nThe current packet's source basis, `main.tex:1265-1416`, does cover the normal\ntrace argument and faithfulness proof.  However, the candidate's own header\nand main-theorem documentation still cite `main.tex:1336-1455`, which excludes\nthe traciality passage at lines 1265-1314.  That stale attribution is a second\nsource-authority defect in the candidate, though not the first acceptance\nblocker.\n\n## Exact declarations and assumptions\n\nThe candidate declares `CornerData`, `FaithfulCornerData`, and\n`IsFaithfulNormalTracialStateOnCorner`.  Its relevant results are:\n\n- `CornerData.cornerTracialOn_vonNeumann`, conditional extension of supplied\n  C-star cyclicity through P49C bounded compressed approximation;\n- `CornerData.tau_tendsto_of_wotTendsto` and `tau_continuous_wot`, vector\n  functional continuity; and\n- `FaithfulCornerData.faithful` and\n  `FaithfulCornerData.isFaithfulNormalTracialState`, conditional dense-set\n  faithfulness and the packaged corner-state conclusion.\n\nBesides complete complex Hilbert-space data, it assumes a norm-closed unital\nrepresented star subalgebra, a self-adjoint idempotent `q` in its bicommutant,\na unit vector fixed by `q`, the supplied `cstar_tracial` premise, a commuting\ncomplementary operator set, and density of the span of `a (b Ω)`.  It does not\nadd a global trace or weight, and P49C's Kaplansky theorem is used rather than\nsupplied.\n\n## Acceptance review\n\n| Classification | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| proved | The quarantined candidate type-checks under the already-built live Lean environment; `FiniteCornerTrace` and `KaplanskyDensity` also build live.  The candidate source has no executable `sorry`, `admit`, user `axiom`, `opaque`, `unsafe`, `implemented_by`, or `native_decide` declaration. |\n| partial | Under its explicit `cstar_tracial`, complement-commutation, and density assumptions, it gives an abstract normal/tracial/faithful vector-functional bridge. |\n| blocked | P49 is not an accepted integrated predecessor, and the candidate replaces its required theorem with a supplied field. |\n| failed | The packet's mathematical target is not met at its stated scope: the exported P50 theorem does not instantiate P49's `finite_corner_trace` and thus does not prove C-star cyclicity from the required finite-codespace system and density input. |\n\n## Plan alignment\n\n- **Package and lane:** P50, Lane G — correct.\n- **Predecessors:** P49 and P49C are declared.  P49C is integrated; P49 is\n  rejected/unintegrated.  The declared dependency condition is not satisfied.\n- **Permitted gate:** the candidate otherwise addresses only corner\n  traciality, vector-functional normality, and conditional faithfulness.\n- **Forbidden claims:** no fullness, central-summand conclusion, global\n  trace/weight, or type-III exclusion was found.  It does not discharge any\n  later gate.\n\n## Verification and cleanup\n\nRun from the live project only:\n\n```text\nlake env lean aristotle_responses/P50-quarantine/.../NormalFaithfulCornerTrace.lean\nlake build AristotleCandidates.FiniteCornerTrace AristotleCandidates.KaplanskyDensity\n```\n\nBoth commands succeeded.  No build, update, or dependency fetch was run in\nthe quarantine snapshot.  No candidate was integrated, no manuscript file was\nmodified, and no commit, push, or new Aristotle submission occurred.  The\npre-existing dirty packet, candidate, and review files remain preserved.\n\n## Adversarial review\n\nArtifact types: math, source-backed, workflow.  The first fatal mathematical\ngap is the supplied `cstar_tracial` premise in place of the mandated P49\ninstantiation; it is independent of compilation.  The review also found the\ncandidate's stale source locator.  No scope expansion or forbidden downstream\nclaim was found.  Residual risk: this closeout does not certify the candidate's\nconditional operator-algebra argument as a manuscript theorem, because its\nload-bearing P49 hypothesis is not established at the packet scope.\n# P47 closeout review — center and finite-projection core\n\n## Decision\n\n**Status: proved at the stated infrastructure scope; queue may advance.**\n\nThe completed Aristotle project was downloaded as\n`aristotle_responses/P47-center-finite-projection-core.tar.gz` (SHA-256\n`51640368062f659201ebae314966a1220fab89b20fa2dfa3c33e4ab364744ea6`) and\nextracted, without building or fetching dependencies, at\n`aristotle_responses/P47-extracted/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p47-80u8nxnx_aristotle/`.\nOnly the packet-authorized module\n`AristotleCandidates/CenterFiniteProjectionCore.lean` was integrated into the\nlive project.  Its SHA-256 is\n`c55831ac16d3dec3d471c25c24159a5c22c79dff1460c586830eadda27da57d8` in both\nthe quarantine snapshot and live project.  The archive and extraction remain\nas raw response records.\n\n## Exact declarations and assumptions\n\nFor a concrete `M : VonNeumannAlgebra H`, with\n`[NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H] [CompleteSpace H]`, the module\ndefines:\n\n- `center`, `IsProjection`, `IsCentralProjection`, and `ProjLe`;\n- `MvNEquiv`, `MvNLe`, and `IsFiniteProjection`;\n- the non-unital compressed algebra `corner`;\n- `IsCentralSupport` as a predicate and `IsFull := IsCentralSupport _ _ 1`.\n\nThe key checked lemmas are `coe_center`, `mem_center_iff`,\n`ProjLe.trans`, `MvNEquiv.trans`, `MvNEquiv.add`, `MvNLe.trans`,\n`IsFiniteProjection.mul_central`, `corner_eq_image`,\n`central_corner_eq_image`, `IsCentralSupport.unique`,\n`IsFull.mul_ne_zero`, `isFull_iff_forall_central`, and\n`IsFull.exists_nonzero_projection`.\n\nNo auxiliary mathematical premise was added.  The only imported project-local\ntheory is the already locally used P36 concrete bicommutant core\n`AristotleCandidates.BicommutantVonNeumannCore`; P47 imports no P47--P61\nsuccessor.  The compression/comparison proofs use the ambient C*-identity for\nbounded operators, not a topology, normality, or factor-classification\nassumption.\n\n## Acceptance review\n\n| Classification | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| proved | The requested concrete algebraic vocabulary and basic center, order, compression, Murray--von Neumann comparison, finite-central-compression, central-support, and fullness lemmas.  In particular, `IsFull.mul_ne_zero` proves that a full projection meets every nonzero central projection nontrivially. |\n| partial | None within P47's stated algebraic target. |\n| blocked | Existence/construction of a central-support projection, projection-tower limits, normality, corner traces, and analytic comparison theory remain for later packets.  `IsCentralSupport` is intentionally only a predicate. |\n| failed | None. |\n\nP47's mathematical target is met at its stated scope.  It does **not** establish\na manuscript theorem, a finite corner for a particular projection, or a\nno-type-III conclusion.\n\n## Plan alignment\n\n- **Package and lane:** P47, Lane G.\n- **Predecessors:** none.  The packet-authorized P36 bicommutant import is\n  already locally present and compiled; it is supporting infrastructure, not\n  a P47--P61 dependency.\n- **Permitted gate:** discharged: the algebraic center/corner/fullness\n  vocabulary required by Lane G is available in the live project.\n- **Forbidden downstream claims:** respected.  The module contains no\n  projection tower, trace/state, global weight, fullness assertion for a\n  manuscript projection, type-III exclusion, normality, spatial tensor\n  factorization, or factor classification.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.CenterFiniteProjectionCore` — passed.\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.BicommutantVonNeumannCore AristotleCandidates.CenterFiniteProjectionCore Formalization` — passed.\n- `lake build` — passed in the already-built live project.\n- `lake env lean /dev/stdin` with `#print axioms` for\n  `IsFull.mul_ne_zero`, `IsFiniteProjection.mul_central`, `MvNLe.trans`,\n  `MvNEquiv.add`, `IsCentralSupport.unique`, `center`, and `corner` — each\n  reports only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`.\n- Placeholder/forbidden-declaration scan of P47 and its direct project import\n  — no `sorry`, `admit`, user `axiom`, `opaque`, `unsafe`, `implemented_by`,\n  or `native_decide` occurrence.\n- Quarantine/live SHA-256 comparison and `git diff --check` — passed.\n\n## Adversarial review\n\nNo acceptance-blocking finding.  The audit verified that the only generic\nfullness conclusion is the conditional algebraic intersection lemma, and that\nthe finite-compression theorem is not combined with it to claim the Lane-G/P51\ncentral finite-projection conclusion.  Residual mathematical risk is limited\nto the explicitly deferred analytic and existence results above; compilation\ndoes not validate those later claims.\n\n## Cleanup and worktree state\n\nKept intentionally: the integrated P47 candidate, its quarantine archive and\nextraction, and this review.  All pre-existing modified and untracked work was\npreserved.  No manuscript file was changed; no commit, push, dependency\nupdate, archive build, or dependency fetch was performed.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,300p' AristotleCandidates/CenterFiniteProjectionCore.lean 2>/dev/null; sed -n '1,320p' AristotleCandidates/NormalFaithfulCornerTrace.lean 2>/dev/null; rg -n \\\"axiom|sorry|admit|opaque|unsafe|FullFinite|finite|full|typeIII|zq\\\" AristotleCandidates/CenterFiniteProjectionCore.lean AristotleCandidates/NormalFaithfulCornerTrace.lean\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,300p' AristotleCandidates/CenterFiniteProjectionCore.lean 2>/dev/null; sed -n '1,320p' AristotleCandidates/NormalFaithfulCornerTrace.lean 2>/dev/null; rg -n \\\"axiom|sorry|admit|opaque|unsafe|FullFinite|finite|full|typeIII|zq\\\" AristotleCandidates/CenterFiniteProjectionCore.lean AristotleCandidates/NormalFaithfulCornerTrace.lean\"","aggregated_output":"import Mathlib.Analysis.VonNeumannAlgebra.Basic\nimport AristotleCandidates.BicommutantVonNeumannCore\n\n/-!\n# Center, projections, corners, central support and fullness\n\nThis file develops, for Mathlib's *concrete* von Neumann algebras\n`M : VonNeumannAlgebra H` (star subalgebras of `H →L[ℂ] H` equal to their own double\ncommutant), the algebraic vocabulary of Murray--von Neumann comparison theory:\n\n* `VonNeumannAlgebra.center` — the center `M ∩ M'`, again a concrete von Neumann algebra;\n* `VonNeumannAlgebra.IsProjection`, `VonNeumannAlgebra.IsCentralProjection` — (central)\n  star projections belonging to `M` (Mathlib's `IsStarProjection` is reused);\n* `VonNeumannAlgebra.ProjLe` — the order `p ≤ q` on projections, written algebraically as\n  `p * q = p ∧ q * p = p`;\n* `VonNeumannAlgebra.MvNEquiv`, `VonNeumannAlgebra.MvNLe` — Murray--von Neumann equivalence\n  and subequivalence of projections implemented by a partial isometry in `M`;\n* `VonNeumannAlgebra.IsFiniteProjection` — a projection with no proper equivalent\n  subprojection;\n* `VonNeumannAlgebra.corner` — the compressed algebra `p M p`, as a non-unital star\n  subalgebra of `H →L[ℂ] H`;\n* `VonNeumannAlgebra.IsCentralSupport` and `VonNeumannAlgebra.IsFull` — the central support\n  of a projection (as a *predicate*, so that no completeness of the projection lattice is\n  needed) and fullness, i.e. central support `1`.\n\nThe main \"central intersection\" statement proved here is\n`VonNeumannAlgebra.IsFull.mul_ne_zero`: a full projection meets every nonzero central\nprojection nontrivially, together with its converse\n`VonNeumannAlgebra.isFull_iff_forall_central`.\n\nThe main comparison lemmas are `VonNeumannAlgebra.MvNEquiv.add` (orthogonal sums of\nequivalences), `VonNeumannAlgebra.MvNLe.trans` (transitivity of subequivalence, via\n`VonNeumannAlgebra.conj_isProjection_of_projLe`) and the compression lemma\n`VonNeumannAlgebra.IsFiniteProjection.mul_central` (a central compression of a finite\nprojection is finite).\n\n## Scope: algebra versus analysis\n\nEverything in this file is **algebraic**.  No operator topology, no normality, no\nsemifiniteness, and no classification of factors is used or asserted.  The only place where\na genuinely *metric* fact about `H →L[ℂ] H` enters is\n`VonNeumannAlgebra.mul_star_mul_self_eq_self` (and the results depending on it, namely that\nthe right endpoint of a Murray--von Neumann equivalence is again a projection, orthogonal\nadditivity of equivalences, and the transitivity of `MvNLe`), which uses the C*-identity\nthrough\n`CStarRing.star_mul_self_eq_zero_iff : star x * x = 0 ↔ x = 0`.  That is a norm identity\navailable in the pinned Mathlib for `H →L[ℂ] H`; it is *not* an operator-topology or a\nvon Neumann density statement.\n\nIn particular this file contains **no** projection tower, no corner trace, no weight, and no\ntype classification; those belong to later developments.\n-/\n\nuniverse u\n\nvariable {H : Type u} [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H] [CompleteSpace H]\n\nnamespace VonNeumannAlgebra\n\n/-! ### The center of a concrete von Neumann algebra -/\n\n/-- The center `M ∩ M'` of a concrete von Neumann algebra, again a concrete von Neumann\nalgebra.  It is realised as the commutant of `M ∪ M'`, which makes the double-commutant\ncondition automatic. -/\nnoncomputable def center (M : VonNeumannAlgebra H) : VonNeumannAlgebra H where\n  toStarSubalgebra :=\n    StarSubalgebra.centralizer ℂ ((M : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)) ∪ (M.commutant : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)))\n  centralizer_centralizer' := by\n    have h : ((StarSubalgebra.centralizer ℂ\n          ((M : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)) ∪ (M.commutant : Set (H →L[ℂ] H))) :\n            StarSubalgebra ℂ (H →L[ℂ] H)) : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)) =\n        Set.centralizer ((M : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)) ∪ (M.commutant : Set (H →L[ℂ] H))) := by\n      rw [StarSubalgebra.coe_centralizer, Set.union_star, StarMemClass.star_coe_eq,\n        StarMemClass.star_coe_eq, Set.union_self]\n    show Set.centralizer (Set.centralizer\n        ((StarSubalgebra.centralizer ℂ\n          ((M : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)) ∪ (M.commutant : Set (H →L[ℂ] H))) :\n            StarSubalgebra ℂ (H →L[ℂ] H)) : Set (H →L[ℂ] H))) = _\n    rw [h, Set.centralizer_centralizer_centralizer]\n    exact h.symm\n\n@[simp]\ntheorem coe_center (M : VonNeumannAlgebra H) :\n    (M.center : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)) =\n      (M : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)) ∩ Set.centralizer (M : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)) := by\n  show ((StarSubalgebra.centralizer ℂ\n      ((M : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)) ∪ (M.commutant : Set (H →L[ℂ] H))) :\n        StarSubalgebra ℂ (H →L[ℂ] H)) : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)) = _\n  rw [StarSubalgebra.coe_centralizer, Set.union_star, StarMemClass.star_coe_eq,\n    StarMemClass.star_coe_eq, Set.union_self, Set.centralizer_union, coe_commutant,\n    M.centralizer_centralizer, Set.inter_comm]\n\ntheorem mem_center_iff {M : VonNeumannAlgebra H} {x : H →L[ℂ] H} :\n    x ∈ M.center ↔ x ∈ M ∧ ∀ y ∈ M, y * x = x * y := by\n  rw [← SetLike.mem_coe, coe_center]\n  exact Iff.rfl\n\ntheorem mem_of_mem_center {M : VonNeumannAlgebra H} {x : H →L[ℂ] H} (hx : x ∈ M.center) :\n    x ∈ M := (mem_center_iff.mp hx).1\n\ntheorem center_commute {M : VonNeumannAlgebra H} {x y : H →L[ℂ] H} (hx : x ∈ M.center)\n    (hy : y ∈ M) : Commute x y :=\n  ((mem_center_iff.mp hx).2 y hy).symm\n\ntheorem center_le (M : VonNeumannAlgebra H) :\n    (M.center : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)) ⊆ (M : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)) := fun _ hx => mem_of_mem_center hx\n\ntheorem center_le_commutant (M : VonNeumannAlgebra H) :\n    (M.center : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)) ⊆ (M.commutant : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)) := by\n  rw [coe_center, coe_commutant]\n  exact Set.inter_subset_right\n\n/-- The center of `M` is the center of its commutant. -/\ntheorem center_commutant (M : VonNeumannAlgebra H) : M.commutant.center = M.center := by\n  refine SetLike.coe_injective ?_\n  rw [coe_center, coe_center, coe_commutant, M.centralizer_centralizer, Set.inter_comm]\n\n/-! ### Projections and central projections -/\n\n/-- A *projection of `M`* is a self-adjoint idempotent belonging to `M`. -/\ndef IsProjection (M : VonNeumannAlgebra H) (p : H →L[ℂ] H) : Prop :=\n  IsStarProjection p ∧ p ∈ M\n\n/-- A *central projection* of `M` is a projection lying in the center of `M`. -/\ndef IsCentralProjection (M : VonNeumannAlgebra H) (z : H →L[ℂ] H) : Prop :=\n  IsStarProjection z ∧ z ∈ M.center\n\nnamespace IsProjection\n\nvariable {M : VonNeumannAlgebra H} {p q : H →L[ℂ] H}\n\ntheorem isStarProjection (hp : M.IsProjection p) : IsStarProjection p := hp.1\n\ntheorem mem (hp : M.IsProjection p) : p ∈ M := hp.2\n\ntheorem mul_self (hp : M.IsProjection p) : p * p = p := hp.1.isIdempotentElem\n\ntheorem star_eq (hp : M.IsProjection p) : star p = p := hp.1.isSelfAdjoint.star_eq\n\ntheorem one_sub (hp : M.IsProjection p) : M.IsProjection (1 - p) :=\n  ⟨hp.1.one_sub, sub_mem (one_mem M) hp.2⟩\n\nend IsProjection\n\ntheorem isProjection_zero (M : VonNeumannAlgebra H) : M.IsProjection 0 :=\n  ⟨IsStarProjection.zero _, zero_mem M⟩\n\ntheorem isProjection_one (M : VonNeumannAlgebra H) : M.IsProjection 1 :=\n  ⟨IsStarProjection.one _, one_mem M⟩\n\nnamespace IsCentralProjection\n\nvariable {M : VonNeumannAlgebra H} {z w : H →L[ℂ] H}\n\ntheorem isStarProjection (hz : M.IsCentralProjection z) : IsStarProjection z := hz.1\n\ntheorem mem_center (hz : M.IsCentralProjection z) : z ∈ M.center := hz.2\n\n/-- A central projection is in particular a projection of `M`. -/\ntheorem isProjection (hz : M.IsCentralProjection z) : M.IsProjection z :=\n  ⟨hz.1, mem_of_mem_center hz.2⟩\n\ntheorem commute (hz : M.IsCentralProjection z) {x : H →L[ℂ] H} (hx : x ∈ M) : z * x = x * z :=\n  (center_commute hz.2 hx).eq\n\ntheorem one_sub (hz : M.IsCentralProjection z) : M.IsCentralProjection (1 - z) := by\n  refine ⟨hz.1.one_sub, mem_center_iff.mpr ⟨sub_mem (one_mem M) (mem_of_mem_center hz.2), ?_⟩⟩\n  intro y hy\n  simp [sub_mul, mul_sub, hz.commute hy]\n\ntheorem mul (hz : M.IsCentralProjection z) (hw : M.IsCentralProjection w) :\n    M.IsCentralProjection (z * w) := by\n  have hcomm : Commute z w := center_commute hz.2 (mem_of_mem_center hw.2)\n  refine ⟨hz.1.mul hw.1 hcomm, mem_center_iff.mpr\n    ⟨mul_mem (mem_of_mem_center hz.2) (mem_of_mem_center hw.2), fun y hy => ?_⟩⟩\n  rw [← mul_assoc, ← hz.commute hy, mul_assoc, ← hw.commute hy, ← mul_assoc]\n\nend IsCentralProjection\n\ntheorem isCentralProjection_zero (M : VonNeumannAlgebra H) : M.IsCentralProjection 0 :=\n  ⟨IsStarProjection.zero _, zero_mem M.center⟩\n\ntheorem isCentralProjection_one (M : VonNeumannAlgebra H) : M.IsCentralProjection 1 :=\n  ⟨IsStarProjection.one _, one_mem M.center⟩\n\n/-! ### The order on projections -/\n\nsection Order\n\nomit [CompleteSpace H]\n\n/-- The usual order on projections, written purely algebraically: `p ≤ q` means that `q` acts\nas the identity on the range of `p`.  For star projections the two equations are equivalent,\nsee `VonNeumannAlgebra.projLe_of_mul_eq_left`. -/\ndef ProjLe (p q : H →L[ℂ] H) : Prop := p * q = p ∧ q * p = p\n\nnamespace ProjLe\n\nvariable {p q r : H →L[ℂ] H}\n\ntheorem mul_right (h : ProjLe p q) : p * q = p := h.1\n\ntheorem mul_left (h : ProjLe p q) : q * p = p := h.2\n\ntheorem refl (hp : IsIdempotentElem p) : ProjLe p p := ⟨hp, hp⟩\n\ntheorem trans (hpq : ProjLe p q) (hqr : ProjLe q r) : ProjLe p r :=\n  ⟨by rw [← hpq.1, mul_assoc, hqr.1], by rw [← hpq.2, ← mul_assoc, hqr.2]⟩\n\ntheorem antisymm (hpq : ProjLe p q) (hqp : ProjLe q p) : p = q := by\n  rw [← hpq.1, hqp.2]\n\nend ProjLe\n\ntheorem zero_projLe (p : H →L[ℂ] H) : ProjLe 0 p := by simp [ProjLe]\n\ntheorem projLe_one (p : H →L[ℂ] H) : ProjLe p 1 := by\n  simp [ProjLe]\n\ntheorem ProjLe.eq_zero_of_le_zero {p : H →L[ℂ] H} (h : ProjLe p 0) : p = 0 := by\n  simpa using h.1.symm\n\nend Order\n\n/-- For star projections, `p * q = p` already implies `q * p = p`. -/\ntheorem projLe_of_mul_eq_left {p q : H →L[ℂ] H} (hp : IsStarProjection p)\n    (hq : IsStarProjection q) (h : p * q = p) : ProjLe p q := by\n  refine ⟨h, ?_⟩\n  have := congrArg star h\n  rwa [star_mul, hp.isSelfAdjoint.star_eq, hq.isSelfAdjoint.star_eq] at this\n\ntheorem projLe_of_mul_eq_right {p q : H →L[ℂ] H} (hp : IsStarProjection p)\n    (hq : IsStarProjection q) (h : q * p = p) : ProjLe p q :=\n  ⟨by\n    have := congrArg star h\n    rwa [star_mul, hp.isSelfAdjoint.star_eq, hq.isSelfAdjoint.star_eq] at this, h⟩\n\n\n/-- If `p ≤ q` are projections of `M`, then `q - p` is a projection of `M`. -/\ntheorem IsProjection.sub {M : VonNeumannAlgebra H} {p q : H →L[ℂ] H} (hp : M.IsProjection p)\n    (hq : M.IsProjection q) (hpq : ProjLe p q) : M.IsProjection (q - p) :=\n  ⟨hp.1.sub_of_mul_eq_left hq.1 hpq.1, sub_mem hq.2 hp.2⟩\n\n/-- The product of a central projection with a projection of `M` is a projection of `M`,\ndominated by both factors. -/\ntheorem IsCentralProjection.mul_isProjection {M : VonNeumannAlgebra H} {z p : H →L[ℂ] H}\n    (hz : M.IsCentralProjection z) (hp : M.IsProjection p) : M.IsProjection (z * p) :=\n  ⟨hz.1.mul hp.1 (center_commute hz.2 hp.2), mul_mem (mem_of_mem_center hz.2) hp.2⟩\n\ntheorem IsCentralProjection.mul_projLe_right {M : VonNeumannAlgebra H} {z p : H →L[ℂ] H}\n    (hz : M.IsCentralProjection z) (hp : M.IsProjection p) : ProjLe (z * p) p := by\n  have hc : z * p = p * z := hz.commute hp.2\n  constructor\n  · rw [mul_assoc, hp.mul_self]\n  · rw [← mul_assoc, ← hc, mul_assoc, hp.mul_self]\n\ntheorem IsCentralProjection.mul_projLe_left {M : VonNeumannAlgebra H} {z p : H →L[ℂ] H}\n    (hz : M.IsCentralProjection z) (hp : M.IsProjection p) : ProjLe (z * p) z := by\n  have hc : z * p = p * z := hz.commute hp.2\n  constructor\n  · rw [mul_assoc, ← hc, ← mul_assoc, hz.1.isIdempotentElem]\n  · rw [← mul_assoc, hz.1.isIdempotentElem]\n\n\n/-! ### Partial isometries and Murray--von Neumann comparison -/\n\n/-- If `star v * v` is idempotent, then `v` is a partial isometry: it acts as the identity\nafter compression by `star v * v`.\n\nThis is the one place in this file where a *metric* fact about `H →L[ℂ] H` is used, namely\nthe C*-identity in the form `CStarRing.star_mul_self_eq_zero_iff`. -/\ntheorem mul_star_mul_self_eq_self {v : H →L[ℂ] H} (h : IsIdempotentElem (star v * v)) :\n    v * (star v * v) = v := by\n  obtain ⟨p, hp⟩ : ∃ p, star v * v = p := ⟨_, rfl⟩\n  rw [hp] at h ⊢\n  have hpp : p * p = p := h\n  have hps : star p = p := by rw [← hp, star_mul, star_star]\n  have hstar : star (v - v * p) = star v - p * star v := by rw [star_sub, star_mul, hps]\n  have expand : star (v - v * p) * (v - v * p)\n      = star v * v - star v * v * p - p * (star v * v) + p * (star v * v) * p := by\n    rw [hstar]; noncomm_ring\n  rw [hp] at expand\n  simp only [hpp] at expand\n  have key : star (v - v * p) * (v - v * p) = 0 := by rw [expand]; abel\n  have hv : v - v * p = 0 := (CStarRing.star_mul_self_eq_zero_iff _).mp key\n  exact (sub_eq_zero.mp hv).symm\n\n/-- **Murray--von Neumann equivalence**: `p` and `q` are equivalent when there is a partial\nisometry `v ∈ M` with `star v * v = p` and `v * star v = q`. -/\ndef MvNEquiv (M : VonNeumannAlgebra H) (p q : H →L[ℂ] H) : Prop :=\n  ∃ v ∈ M, star v * v = p ∧ v * star v = q\n\n/-- **Murray--von Neumann subequivalence**: `p` is equivalent to a subprojection of `q`. -/\ndef MvNLe (M : VonNeumannAlgebra H) (p q : H →L[ℂ] H) : Prop :=\n  ∃ r, M.IsProjection r ∧ ProjLe r q ∧ M.MvNEquiv p r\n\nnamespace MvNEquiv\n\nvariable {M : VonNeumannAlgebra H} {p q r : H →L[ℂ] H}\n\nimport Mathlib\nimport AristotleCandidates.FiniteCornerTrace\nimport AristotleCandidates.KaplanskyDensity\n\n/-!\n# P50 — the faithful normal tracial state on the von Neumann corner `q M_Γ q`\n\n**Source basis:** `main.tex:1265-1417` (Proposition `prop:normal-trace` and\nProposition `prop:faithful`).\n\n**Plan alignment.**  Package `P50`, lane `G`.  Predecessors used: `P49`\n(`AristotleCandidates.FiniteCornerTrace`) for the C⋆-level cyclicity of the\ncompressed vector functional, and `P49C`\n(`AristotleCandidates.KaplanskyDensity`) for the *proved* Kaplansky bounded\napproximation and the bounded compressed product convergence.  Through those,\n`P47`, `P48`, `P49A` and `P49B` are used transitively.\n\nThe gate discharged here is exactly the manuscript's Propositions\n`prop:normal-trace` and `prop:faithful`: the compressed vector functional\n`tau_q` extends from the compressed quasi-local C⋆-algebra to the whole von\nNeumann corner `q M_Γ q`, and is there a **faithful normal finite tracial\nstate** — unital and positive, hence a state and not merely a weight.\n\n**Forbidden downstream claims, not made anywhere in this file.**  No fullness\nof `q`, no finiteness of `q` as a projection, no statement about central\nsummands or central supports, no global trace or weight on `M_Γ`, and no\ntype-III exclusion.\n\n## What is proved\n\n* `cornerTau_continuous_wot`, `tauVec_tendsto_of_stronglyTendsto`,\n  `cornerTau_tendsto_of_stronglyTendsto`, `cornerTau_continuous_sot`, and\n  `cornerTau_tendsto_sum_of_stronglyTendsto` — **normality**.  The compressed\n  functional is continuous for the weak operator topology, hence ultraweakly\n  continuous in this vector-functional form; the additional strong-operator\n  results carry strong limits and partial sums to limits.  This is the\n  manuscript's \"since `tau_q` is a restriction of a vector functional it is\n  normal\", turned into proved statements about that realization.\n* `cornerTracialOn_bicommutant`, `cornerTracialOn_vonNeumannGenerated` —\n  **traciality on the von Neumann corner**.  Cyclicity of `tau_q` on the\n  compressions of a norm-closed unital star algebra `A` propagates to the\n  compressions of its bicommutant `M = A''`, using the P49C bounded compressed\n  approximants and bounded product convergence.  This is `main.tex:1265-1315`.\n* `norm_star_apply_eq_of_cornerTracial`, `apply_apply_eq_zero_of_apply_eq_zero`,\n  `cornerTau_faithful` — **faithfulness**, from the manuscript's\n  dense-vector/commuting-complement argument (`main.tex:1352-1417`).  The\n  square-root step of the manuscript is replaced by the equivalent and simpler\n  consequence `‖x* Ω‖ = ‖x Ω‖` of traciality; this is a change of proof route\n  only, and it proves the same statement.\n* `IsFaithfulNormalTracialCorner` — the packaged conclusion: `q` is a\n  projection of `M`, and `tau_q` is a unital, positive, tracial, normal and\n  faithful functional on the corner `q M q`.\n* `normal_faithful_corner_trace` — the **exported P50 theorem**.  It takes the\n  P49 compatible finite-codespace system, its decreasing projection tower, the\n  represented C⋆-algebra `A` with its norm-density data, the commuting\n  complement and the dense-vector premise, and produces\n  `IsFaithfulNormalTracialCorner (A'') q Ω` for `q` the tower's `limitProj`.\n  C⋆-level cyclicity is *derived* by instantiating\n  `CompatibleFiniteCodespaceSystem.finite_corner_trace` of P49; it is not an\n  assumption, and neither `CornerTracialOn` nor a Kaplansky-density or\n  bicommutant interface appears among the hypotheses: those are used as proved\n  results of P49/P49B/P49C.\n\n## The remaining non-analytic premises of the exported theorem\n\n1. the finite codespace data `D` of P49 (finite-stage star representations,\n   hermitian idempotent code projections, densities `rho_n = weight n • P_n` of\n   trace one, and the GNS vector-state identity `⟪Ω, pi n x Ω⟫ = Tr(rho_n x)`),\n   together with the stage inclusions;\n2. `hp`: `IsDecreasingProjTower` for the stage projections (`main.tex` Lemma\n   `lema:proj_inequality`) — the same premise as in P49;\n3. `hAclosed`: the represented regional algebra `A = pi_omega(A_Γ)` is a\n   norm-closed unital star subalgebra of `B(H)`, i.e. a represented C⋆-algebra;\n4. `hlocal` and `hAdense`: the finite-stage operators lie in `A`, and `A` is\n   contained in their norm closure — i.e. `A` *is* the quasi-local C⋆-algebra.\n   This is exactly the norm-density input P49 already requires, and which the\n   packet explicitly permits to remain explicit;\n5. `hB`: the represented complementary algebra `B = pi_omega(A_{Γᶜ})` commutes\n   with `A` (`main.tex` eq. `eq:M-commutes-complement`); and\n6. `hdense`: the vectors `pi_omega(b) pi_omega(a) Ω` with `a ∈ A`, `b ∈ B` span\n   a dense subspace of the GNS space (`main.tex` eq. `eq:dense_states`, i.e.\n   cyclicity of the global GNS vector).\n\nStrong closedness of commutants, the double commutant theorem and Kaplansky\ndensity are *used as theorems* (P49A, P49B, P49C), never as hypotheses.\n-/\n\nuniverse u v\n\nopen Filter Topology\n\nnamespace AristotleCandidates\nnamespace NormalFaithfulCornerTrace\n\nopen FiniteCornerTrace ProjectionTower\nopen scoped InnerProductSpace\n\nvariable {H : Type u} [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H] [CompleteSpace H]\n\n/-! ## §1  Normality: the vector-functional realization -/\n\nsection Normality\n\nomit [CompleteSpace H] in\n/-- A strongly convergent net is carried to a convergent net by the vector functional. -/\ntheorem tauVec_tendsto_of_stronglyTendsto {α : Type v} {l : Filter α}\n    {f : α → H →L[ℂ] H} {x : H →L[ℂ] H} (Ω : H)\n    (h : StrongOperator.StronglyTendsto l f x) :\n    Tendsto (fun i => tauVec Ω (f i)) l (𝓝 (tauVec Ω x)) := by\n  have h0 : Tendsto (fun i => f i Ω) l (𝓝 (x Ω)) := h Ω\n  exact ((innerSL ℂ Ω).continuous.tendsto _).comp h0\n\n/-- **Normality, net form.**  The compressed functional `tau_q` carries strong limits of nets to\nlimits.  This is the manuscript's \"`tau_q` is the restriction of a vector functional, hence\nnormal\", proved from that realization. -/\ntheorem cornerTau_tendsto_of_stronglyTendsto {α : Type v} {l : Filter α}\n    {f : α → H →L[ℂ] H} {x : H →L[ℂ] H} (q : H →L[ℂ] H) (Ω : H)\n    (h : StrongOperator.StronglyTendsto l f x) :\n    Tendsto (fun i => cornerTau q Ω (f i)) l (𝓝 (cornerTau q Ω x)) :=\n  tauVec_tendsto_of_stronglyTendsto Ω (h.compress q q)\n\n/-- **Normality, topological form.**  `tau_q` is continuous for the strong operator topology;\na strong-operator continuous linear functional is in particular σ-weakly continuous. -/\ntheorem cornerTau_continuous_sot (q : H →L[ℂ] H) (Ω : H) :\n    Continuous fun T : StrongOperator.SOT H => cornerTau q Ω (StrongOperator.ofSOT T) := by\n  have h1 : Continuous fun T : StrongOperator.SOT H => (StrongOperator.ofSOT T) (q Ω) :=\n    continuous_eval_const (q Ω)\n  exact (innerSL ℂ Ω).continuous.comp (q.continuous.comp h1)\n\n/-- **Normality, weak-operator form.**  The compressed vector functional is\ncontinuous for the weak operator topology.  In particular it is an ultraweakly\ncontinuous, hence normal, functional on every represented von Neumann corner. -/\ntheorem cornerTau_continuous_wot (q : H →L[ℂ] H) (Ω : H) :\n    Continuous fun T : H →WOT[ℂ] H =>\n      cornerTau q Ω ((ContinuousLinearMap.toWOT (RingHom.id ℂ) H H).symm T) := by\n  have h : Continuous fun T : H →WOT[ℂ] H =>\n      ((innerSL ℂ Ω).comp q) (T (q Ω)) :=\n    ContinuousLinearMapWOT.continuous_dual_apply (σ := RingHom.id ℂ) (E := H) (F := H)\n      (q Ω) ((innerSL ℂ Ω).comp q)\n  simpa [cornerTau_apply, ContinuousLinearMap.toWOT_apply] using h\n\n/-- **Normality, countable-additivity form.**  If the partial sums of a sequence of operators\nconverge strongly, then the values of `tau_q` sum to its value at the limit. -/\ntheorem cornerTau_tendsto_sum_of_stronglyTendsto {e : ℕ → H →L[ℂ] H} {x : H →L[ℂ] H}\n    (q : H →L[ℂ] H) (Ω : H)\n    (h : StrongOperator.StronglyTendsto atTop (fun n => ∑ i ∈ Finset.range n, e i) x) :\n    Tendsto (fun n => ∑ i ∈ Finset.range n, cornerTau q Ω (e i)) atTop\n      (𝓝 (cornerTau q Ω x)) := by\n  refine (cornerTau_tendsto_of_stronglyTendsto q Ω h).congr fun n => ?_\n  exact map_sum (cornerTau q Ω) e (Finset.range n)\n\nend Normality\n\n/-! ## §2  Traciality on the von Neumann corner -/\n\nsection Tracial\n\nopen KaplanskyDensity\n\nvariable {q : H →L[ℂ] H} {Ω : H}\n\n/-- **`main.tex:1265-1315`, Proposition `prop:normal-trace`, cyclicity part.**\n\nIf the compressed vector functional is cyclic on the compressions of a norm-closed unital star\nalgebra `A`, then it is cyclic on the compressions of the whole von Neumann algebra `M = A''`.\n\nThe proof is the manuscript's: by the *proved* Kaplansky density theorem of P49C every `x ∈ A''`\nis the strong limit of a uniformly norm-bounded net in `A`; compressions of a uniformly bounded\nnet converge strongly to the compression of the limit; and products of two such nets converge\nstrongly by joint strong continuity of multiplication on bounded sets. -/\ntheorem cornerTracialOn_bicommutant {A : StarSubalgebra ℂ (H →L[ℂ] H)}\n    (hA : IsClosed (A : Set (H →L[ℂ] H))) (hq1 : star q = q) (hq2 : q * q = q)\n    (h : CornerTracialOn q Ω (A : Set (H →L[ℂ] H))) :\n    CornerTracialOn q Ω (Set.centralizer (Set.centralizer (A : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)))) := by\n  intro x hx y hy\n  obtain ⟨l, hne, hc1, hc2⟩ := exists_net_compression_product hA hq1 hq2 hx hy\n  haveI := hne\n  have t1 := tauVec_tendsto_of_stronglyTendsto Ω hc1\n  have t2 := tauVec_tendsto_of_stronglyTendsto Ω hc2\n  have heq : (fun p : {a : H →L[ℂ] H | a ∈ A ∧ ‖a‖ ≤ ‖x‖} ×\n      {b : H →L[ℂ] H | b ∈ A ∧ ‖b‖ ≤ ‖y‖} =>\n        tauVec Ω ((q * (p.1 : H →L[ℂ] H) * q) * (q * (p.2 : H →L[ℂ] H) * q))) =\n      fun p => tauVec Ω ((q * (p.2 : H →L[ℂ] H) * q) * (q * (p.1 : H →L[ℂ] H) * q)) := by\n    funext p\n    exact h _ p.1.2.1 _ p.2.2.1\n  rw [heq] at t1\n  exact tendsto_nhds_unique t1 t2\n\n/-- The same statement for the concrete von Neumann algebra `A''` of the bicommutant core. -/\ntheorem cornerTracialOn_vonNeumannGenerated {A : StarSubalgebra ℂ (H →L[ℂ] H)}\n    (hA : IsClosed (A : Set (H →L[ℂ] H))) (hq1 : star q = q) (hq2 : q * q = q)\n    (h : CornerTracialOn q Ω (A : Set (H →L[ℂ] H))) :\n    CornerTracialOn q Ω ((StarSubalgebra.vonNeumannGenerated A : VonNeumannAlgebra H) :\n      Set (H →L[ℂ] H)) := by\n  rw [StarSubalgebra.coe_vonNeumannGenerated]\n  exact cornerTracialOn_bicommutant hA hq1 hq2 h\n\nend Tracial\n\n/-! ## §3  Faithfulness -/\n\nsection Faithful\n\nvariable {q : H →L[ℂ] H} {Ω : H}\n\ntheorem tauVec_star_mul_self (Ω : H) (u : H →L[ℂ] H) :\n    tauVec Ω (star u * u) = ((‖u Ω‖ : ℝ) : ℂ) ^ 2 := by\n  have h : ((star u * u) Ω) = (star u) (u Ω) := rfl\n  rw [tauVec_apply, h, ContinuousLinearMap.star_eq_adjoint,\n    ContinuousLinearMap.adjoint_inner_right, inner_self_eq_norm_sq_to_K]\n  norm_cast\n\ntheorem tauVec_mul_star_self (Ω : H) (u : H →L[ℂ] H) :\n    tauVec Ω (u * star u) = ((‖(star u) Ω‖ : ℝ) : ℂ) ^ 2 := by\n  have h := tauVec_star_mul_self Ω (star u)\n  rwa [star_star] at h\n\nomit [CompleteSpace H] in\n/-- A corner element is fixed by the compression. -/\ntheorem compress_eq_self {x : H →L[ℂ] H} (hqx : q * x = x) (hxq : x * q = x) :\n    q * x * q = x := by rw [hqx, hxq]\n\n/-- The star of a corner element is again a corner element. -/\ntheorem star_corner {x : H →L[ℂ] H} (hq1 : star q = q) (hqx : q * x = x) (hxq : x * q = x) :\n    q * star x = star x ∧ star x * q = star x := by\n  refine ⟨?_, ?_⟩\n  · have h := congrArg star hxq\n    rwa [star_mul, hq1] at h\n  · have h := congrArg star hqx\n    rwa [star_mul, hq1] at h\n\n/-- **Key consequence of traciality.**  On the corner, `‖x* Ω‖ = ‖x Ω‖`.\n\nThis replaces the manuscript's square-root computation: it is the special case\n`tau_q(x* x) = tau_q(x x*)` of cyclicity, and it is all that the faithfulness argument needs. -/\ntheorem norm_star_apply_eq_of_cornerTracial {M : VonNeumannAlgebra H}\n    (htr : CornerTracialOn q Ω (M : Set (H →L[ℂ] H))) (hq1 : star q = q)\n    {x : H →L[ℂ] H} (hx : x ∈ M) (hqx : q * x = x) (hxq : x * q = x) :\n    ‖(star x) Ω‖ = ‖x Ω‖ := by\n  obtain ⟨hs1, hs2⟩ := star_corner hq1 hqx hxq\n  have hcx : q * x * q = x := compress_eq_self hqx hxq\n  have hcs : q * star x * q = star x := compress_eq_self hs1 hs2\n  have hkey := htr (star x) (star_mem hx) x hx\n  rw [hcx, hcs, tauVec_star_mul_self, tauVec_mul_star_self] at hkey\n  have hr : (‖x Ω‖ : ℝ) ^ 2 = (‖(star x) Ω‖ : ℝ) ^ 2 := by exact_mod_cast hkey\n  nlinarith [norm_nonneg (x Ω), norm_nonneg ((star x) Ω)]\n\n/-- **`main.tex` eq. `eq:xyOmega_zero`.**  A corner element annihilating `Ω` annihilates `y Ω`\nfor every corner element `y`. -/\ntheorem apply_apply_eq_zero_of_apply_eq_zero {M : VonNeumannAlgebra H}\n    (htr : CornerTracialOn q Ω (M : Set (H →L[ℂ] H))) (hq1 : star q = q)\n    {x : H →L[ℂ] H} (hx : x ∈ M) (hqx : q * x = x) (hxq : x * q = x) (hx0 : x Ω = 0)\n    {y : H →L[ℂ] H} (hy : y ∈ M) (hyq : y * q = y) :\n    x (y Ω) = 0 := by\n  have hxs : (star x) Ω = 0 := by\n    have h := norm_star_apply_eq_of_cornerTracial htr hq1 hx hqx hxq\n    rw [hx0] at h\n    exact norm_eq_zero.1 (by simpa using h)\n  have hxy : x * y ∈ M := mul_mem hx hy\n  have h1 : q * (x * y) = x * y := by rw [← mul_assoc, hqx]\n  have h2 : (x * y) * q = x * y := by rw [mul_assoc, hyq]\n  have hnorm := norm_star_apply_eq_of_cornerTracial htr hq1 hxy h1 h2\n  have hstar : (star (x * y)) Ω = 0 := by\n    rw [star_mul]\n    show (star y) ((star x) Ω) = 0\n    rw [hxs, map_zero]\n  rw [hstar] at hnorm\n  exact norm_eq_zero.1 (by simpa using hnorm.symm)\n\n/-- **`main.tex:1352-1417`, Proposition `prop:faithful`.**\n\nLet `q` be a projection of `M = A''` fixing `Ω`, let the compressed vector functional be cyclic\non `M`, let `B` commute with `A`, and let the vectors `b a Ω` with `a ∈ A`, `b ∈ B` span a dense\nsubspace.  Then `tau_q` is faithful on the corner `q M q`. -/\ntheorem cornerTau_faithful {A : StarSubalgebra ℂ (H →L[ℂ] H)}\n    {B : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)} (hB : B ⊆ Set.centralizer (A : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)))\n    (hq1 : star q = q) (hq2 : q * q = q) (hqΩ : q Ω = Ω)\n    (hqM : q ∈ (StarSubalgebra.vonNeumannGenerated A : VonNeumannAlgebra H))\n    (htr : CornerTracialOn q Ω\n      ((StarSubalgebra.vonNeumannGenerated A : VonNeumannAlgebra H) : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)))\n    (hdense : Dense (Submodule.span ℂ\n      {ξ : H | ∃ a ∈ (A : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)), ∃ b ∈ B, ξ = (b * a) Ω} : Set H))\n    {x : H →L[ℂ] H} (hx : x ∈ (StarSubalgebra.vonNeumannGenerated A : VonNeumannAlgebra H))\n    (hqx : q * x = x) (hxq : x * q = x) (h0 : cornerTau q Ω (star x * x) = 0) :\n    x = 0 := by\n  have hsa : IsSelfAdjoint q := hq1\n  -- `tau_q(x* x) = ‖x Ω‖²`, so `x Ω = 0`.\n  have hx0 : x Ω = 0 := by\n    have h := cornerTau_star_mul_self hsa Ω x\n    rw [h0, hqΩ] at h\n    have h3 : (‖x Ω‖ : ℝ) ^ 2 = 0 := by exact_mod_cast h.symm\n    exact norm_eq_zero.1 (by nlinarith [norm_nonneg (x Ω)])\n  -- `x` annihilates `a Ω` for every `a ∈ A`.\n  have hxa : ∀ a ∈ (A : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)), x (a Ω) = 0 := by\n    intro a ha\n    have haM : a ∈ (StarSubalgebra.vonNeumannGenerated A : VonNeumannAlgebra H) :=\n      StarSubalgebra.mem_vonNeumannGenerated_of_mem ha\n    have hy : q * a * q ∈ (StarSubalgebra.vonNeumannGenerated A : VonNeumannAlgebra H) :=\n      mul_mem (mul_mem hqM haM) hqM\n    have h2 : (q * a * q) * q = q * a * q := by\n      calc (q * a * q) * q = q * a * (q * q) := by noncomm_ring\n        _ = q * a * q := by rw [hq2]\n    have hzero := apply_apply_eq_zero_of_apply_eq_zero htr hq1 hx hqx hxq hx0 hy h2\n    have hval : (q * a * q) Ω = q (a Ω) := by\n      show q (a (q Ω)) = q (a Ω)\n      rw [hqΩ]\n    rw [hval] at hzero\n    have hxq' : ∀ z : H, x (q z) = x z := fun z =>\n      congrArg (fun t : H →L[ℂ] H => t z) hxq\n    rwa [hxq'] at hzero\n  -- `x` commutes with the complementary algebra `B`.\n  have hxc : ∀ b ∈ B, b * x = x * b := fun b hb =>\n    StarSubalgebra.mem_vonNeumannGenerated_iff.1 hx b (hB hb)\n  -- `x` annihilates a dense set of vectors, hence vanishes.\n  refine ContinuousLinearMap.ext_on hdense ?_\n  rintro ξ ⟨a, ha, b, hb, rfl⟩\n  have hval : x ((b * a) Ω) = (x * b) (a Ω) := rfl\n  have : x ((b * a) Ω) = 0 := by\n    rw [hval, ← hxc b hb]\n    show b (x (a Ω)) = 0\nAristotleCandidates/NormalFaithfulCornerTrace.lean:21:Neumann corner `q M_Γ q`, and is there a **faithful normal finite tracial\nAristotleCandidates/NormalFaithfulCornerTrace.lean:24:**Forbidden downstream claims, not made anywhere in this file.**  No fullness\nAristotleCandidates/NormalFaithfulCornerTrace.lean:25:of `q`, no finiteness of `q` as a projection, no statement about central\nAristotleCandidates/NormalFaithfulCornerTrace.lean:54:  P49 compatible finite-codespace system, its decreasing projection tower, the\nAristotleCandidates/NormalFaithfulCornerTrace.lean:59:  `CompatibleFiniteCodespaceSystem.finite_corner_trace` of P49; it is not an\nAristotleCandidates/NormalFaithfulCornerTrace.lean:66:1. the finite codespace data `D` of P49 (finite-stage star representations,\nAristotleCandidates/NormalFaithfulCornerTrace.lean:74:4. `hlocal` and `hAdense`: the finite-stage operators lie in `A`, and `A` is\nAristotleCandidates/NormalFaithfulCornerTrace.lean:328:/-- **A faithful normal finite tracial state on the corner `q M q`.**\nAristotleCandidates/NormalFaithfulCornerTrace.lean:335:* `unital`, `positive` — `tau_q` is a *state* (finite and normalized), not a weight;\nAristotleCandidates/NormalFaithfulCornerTrace.lean:398:* `D`, the compatible finite-codespace system of P49, with GNS vector `Ω`;\nAristotleCandidates/NormalFaithfulCornerTrace.lean:401:  finite-stage operators (`hlocal`) and contained in their norm closure (`hAdense`) — the\nAristotleCandidates/NormalFaithfulCornerTrace.lean:407:vector functional `tau_q` is a faithful normal finite tracial state on `q M q`.\nAristotleCandidates/NormalFaithfulCornerTrace.lean:410:`CompatibleFiniteCodespaceSystem.finite_corner_trace` of P49.  Kaplansky density and the\nAristotleCandidates/NormalFaithfulCornerTrace.lean:438:    D.finite_corner_trace hp (A : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)) hAdense\nAristotleCandidates/NormalFaithfulCornerTrace.lean:457:The exported theorem bundles several premises at once (finite codespace data, a decreasing\nAristotleCandidates/NormalFaithfulCornerTrace.lean:458:projection tower, a norm-closed represented algebra squeezed between the finite stages and their\nAristotleCandidates/CenterFiniteProjectionCore.lean:5:# Center, projections, corners, central support and fullness\nAristotleCandidates/CenterFiniteProjectionCore.lean:24:  needed) and fullness, i.e. central support `1`.\nAristotleCandidates/CenterFiniteProjectionCore.lean:27:`VonNeumannAlgebra.IsFull.mul_ne_zero`: a full projection meets every nonzero central\nAristotleCandidates/CenterFiniteProjectionCore.lean:34:`VonNeumannAlgebra.IsFiniteProjection.mul_central` (a central compression of a finite\nAristotleCandidates/CenterFiniteProjectionCore.lean:35:projection is finite).\nAristotleCandidates/CenterFiniteProjectionCore.lean:40:semifiniteness, and no classification of factors is used or asserted.  The only place where\nAristotleCandidates/CenterFiniteProjectionCore.lean:399:/-- A projection of `M` is **finite** when it is not Murray--von Neumann equivalent to a\nAristotleCandidates/CenterFiniteProjectionCore.lean:468:/-- A central compression of a finite projection is finite. -/\nAristotleCandidates/CenterFiniteProjectionCore.lean:479:  have hzq : z * q = q := (hqzp.trans (hz.mul_projLe_left hpproj)).2\nAristotleCandidates/CenterFiniteProjectionCore.lean:482:    rw [hp', ← mul_assoc, mul_sub, mul_one, hqz, hzq, sub_self, zero_mul]\nAristotleCandidates/CenterFiniteProjectionCore.lean:605:/-! ### Central support and fullness -/\nAristotleCandidates/CenterFiniteProjectionCore.lean:616:/-- A projection is **full** when its central support is `1`. -/\nAristotleCandidates/CenterFiniteProjectionCore.lean:642:/-- A full projection meets every nonzero central projection nontrivially: this is the basic\nAristotleCandidates/CenterFiniteProjectionCore.lean:653:/-- Conversely, a projection meeting every nonzero central projection is full. -/\nAristotleCandidates/CenterFiniteProjectionCore.lean:664:/-- Sanity checks: `1` is full and `0` has central support `0`. -/\nAristotleCandidates/CenterFiniteProjectionCore.lean:675:/-- For a full projection `p` of `M` and a nonzero central projection `z`, the compression\nAristotleCandidates/CenterFiniteProjectionCore.lean:678:    (hp : M.IsProjection p) (hfull : M.IsFull p) (hz : M.IsCentralProjection z) (hz0 : z ≠ 0) :\nAristotleCandidates/CenterFiniteProjectionCore.lean:680:  ⟨hz.mul_isProjection hp, hfull.mul_ne_zero hz hz0, hz.mul_projLe_left hp,\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
