{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba aristotle_tasks/P51-full-finite-corner-central-exclusion.md | sed -n '1,120p'; nl -ba aristotle_responses/P51-full-finite-corner-central-exclusion-10f2fe5c-f7631f0b-quarantine/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p51-_l52ps0z_aristotle/AristotleCandidates/FullFiniteCornerCentralExclusion.lean | sed -n '1,390p'; git status --short\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# P51 — full finite corner and central type-III exclusion\n     2\t\n     3\t## Context declaration\n     4\t\n     5\t- **Source basis:** `main.tex:1456-1536`.\n     6\t\n     7\t## Plan alignment\n     8\t\n     9\t- **Package and lane:** `P51`; Lane `G`.\n    10\t- **Predecessors:** `P47`, `P50`, both integrated and locally audited before submission.\n    11\t- **Gate discharged:** prove `q` finite and full, then produce a nonzero finite\n    12\t  projection in every nonzero central summand and state the type-III obstruction.\n    13\t- **Forbidden downstream claims:** no direct integral, no trivial-center claim,\n    14\t  no global faithful normal semifinite weight, and no Lane-H tensor factorization.\n    15\t\n    16\t## Mathematical target\n    17\t\n    18\tCreate only `AristotleCandidates/FullFiniteCornerCentralExclusion.lean`. Use the\n    19\tP50 faithful normal tracial state to prove finiteness of `q`; formalize the\n    20\tmanuscript fullness argument; and prove that for every nonzero central projection\n    21\t`z`, the projection `zq` is nonzero and finite in the corner/summand `z M_Gamma`.\n    22\tDefine or reuse a project-local predicate expressing the resulting obstruction\n    23\tto a type-III central summand. A finite-dimensional subalgebra is not sufficient.\n    24\t\n    25\t## Auxiliary assumptions\n    26\t\n    27\tState every fullness or comparison premise not derived from the manuscript data.\n    28\tDo not assume or manufacture a global trace.\n    29\t\n    30\t## Files and imports\n    31\t\n    32\tCreate only `AristotleCandidates/FullFiniteCornerCentralExclusion.lean`; import\n    33\tP47 and P50.\n    34\t\n    35\t## Acceptance criteria\n    36\t\n    37\t`lake build AristotleCandidates.FullFiniteCornerCentralExclusion` succeeds\n    38\twithout forbidden declarations. The response must identify the exact theorem\n    39\twhose conclusion contains the nonzero finite projection `zq`.\n     1\timport Mathlib\n     2\timport AristotleCandidates.CenterFiniteProjectionCore\n     3\timport AristotleCandidates.NormalFaithfulCornerTrace\n     4\t\n     5\t/-!\n     6\t# P51 — finiteness and fullness of `q`, and exclusion of type-III central summands\n     7\t\n     8\t**Source basis:** `main.tex:1456-1536` (Lemma `lem:finite_corner_finite_global`,\n     9\tProposition `prop:fullness`, Theorem `thm:finite_projections_exist`).\n    10\t\n    11\t**Plan alignment.**  Package `P51`, lane `G`.  Predecessors used: `P47`\n    12\t(`AristotleCandidates.CenterFiniteProjectionCore`) for the algebraic comparison\n    13\tvocabulary — projections, `ProjLe`, Murray–von Neumann equivalence, finiteness,\n    14\tcorners, central support and fullness — and `P50`\n    15\t(`AristotleCandidates.NormalFaithfulCornerTrace`) for the faithful normal\n    16\ttracial state `tau_q` on the von Neumann corner `q M_Γ q`.  Through those,\n    17\t`P48`, `P49`, `P49A`, `P49B` and `P49C` are used transitively.\n    18\t\n    19\tThe gate discharged here is exactly the manuscript's\n    20\t\n    21\t* Lemma `lem:finite_corner_finite_global` (`main.tex:1447-1451`): a faithful\n    22\t  tracial functional on `q M q` forces `q` to be a **finite projection of `M`**;\n    23\t* Proposition `prop:fullness` (`main.tex:1475-1509`): `q` is **full** in `M_Γ`;\n    24\t* Theorem `thm:finite_projections_exist` (`main.tex:1511-1536`): for every\n    25\t  nonzero central projection `z`, the operator `zq` is a **nonzero finite\n    26\t  projection lying in the central summand `z M_Γ`**, so that summand is not\n    27\t  type III.\n    28\t\n    29\t**Forbidden downstream claims, not made anywhere in this file.**  No direct\n    30\tintegral, no trivial-center claim, no global faithful normal semifinite weight\n    31\tor trace on `M_Γ`, and no Lane-H tensor factorization.\n    32\t\n    33\t## The exact theorem containing the nonzero finite projection `zq`\n    34\t\n    35\t`AristotleCandidates.FullFiniteCornerCentralExclusion.central_summand_nonzero_finite_projection`\n    36\tis the theorem whose conclusion contains the nonzero finite projection `z * q`:\n    37\tit asserts simultaneously `z * q ≠ 0`, `M.IsFiniteProjection (z * q)` (finiteness\n    38\trelative to all of `M`), `z * q ∈ centralSummand M z`, and\n    39\t`IsFiniteProjectionIn (centralSummand M z) (z * q)` (finiteness relative to the\n    40\tsummand itself).  Its packaged corollary\n    41\t`not_isTypeIIILike_centralSummand` states the type-III obstruction\n    42\t`¬ IsTypeIIILike (centralSummand M z)`, and\n    43\t`full_finite_corner_central_exclusion` is the exported form taking the P50 input\n    44\tdata.\n    45\t\n    46\t## Auxiliary assumptions\n    47\t\n    48\tBeyond the P50 data, exactly two premises are used, both already appearing in\n    49\tP50 and both manuscript clauses:\n    50\t\n    51\t* `hB : B ⊆ Set.centralizer A` — the represented complementary algebra\n    52\t  `pi_omega(A_{Γᶜ})` commutes with `A = pi_omega(A_Γ)` (`main.tex`\n    53\t  eq. `eq:M-commutes-complement`); and\n    54\t* `hdense` — the vectors `pi_omega(b) pi_omega(a) Ω` span a dense subspace\n    55\t  (`main.tex` eq. `eq:dense_states`).\n    56\t\n    57\tNo global trace or weight is assumed or manufactured; the only tracial datum is\n    58\tthe P50 corner state `tau_q`.\n    59\t\n    60\t## Relative finiteness\n    61\t\n    62\tMathlib's `VonNeumannAlgebra H` is a *unital* algebra of operators on all of `H`,\n    63\tso the reduced algebra `z M` (which is unital only on `z H`) is treated here as a\n    64\t**set** of operators, `centralSummand M z`, with the set-relative comparison\n    65\tpredicates `MvNEquivIn`, `IsFiniteProjectionIn` and the type-III obstruction\n    66\t`IsTypeIIILike`.  `isFiniteProjectionIn_of_isFiniteProjection` is the general\n    67\tmonotonicity statement corresponding to the manuscript's last step (\"`zq` is\n    68\tfinite with respect to `z M_Γ`\"): finiteness with respect to a larger set of\n    69\tpartial isometries is the stronger property.\n    70\t-/\n    71\t\n    72\tuniverse u\n    73\t\n    74\tnamespace AristotleCandidates\n    75\tnamespace FullFiniteCornerCentralExclusion\n    76\t\n    77\topen Filter Topology\n    78\topen FiniteCornerTrace ProjectionTower NormalFaithfulCornerTrace\n    79\topen scoped InnerProductSpace\n    80\t\n    81\tvariable {H : Type u} [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H] [CompleteSpace H]\n    82\t\n    83\t/-! ## §1  A faithful tracial corner state makes `q` a finite projection\n    84\t\n    85\tThis is `main.tex` Lemma `lem:finite_corner_finite_global`: the manuscript's proof of\n    86\tfiniteness of `q` uses only that `tau_q` is a faithful tracial functional on `q M q`.\n    87\t-/\n    88\t\n    89\tsection Finiteness\n    90\t\n    91\t/-- A partial isometry implementing `q ~ r` with `r ≤ q` lies in the corner `q M q`. -/\n    92\ttheorem mem_corner_of_mvNEquiv_projLe {M : VonNeumannAlgebra H} {q r v : H →L[ℂ] H}\n    93\t    (hqsa : IsSelfAdjoint q) (hqidem : IsIdempotentElem q) (hridem : IsIdempotentElem r)\n    94\t    (hv : v ∈ M) (hv1 : star v * v = q) (hv2 : v * star v = r)\n    95\t    (hrq : VonNeumannAlgebra.ProjLe r q) :\n    96\t    v ∈ M.corner hqsa ∧ star v ∈ M.corner hqsa := by\n    97\t  have hvq : v * q = v := by\n    98\t    have := VonNeumannAlgebra.mul_star_mul_self_eq_self (v := v) (by rw [hv1]; exact hqidem)\n    99\t    rwa [hv1] at this\n   100\t  have hrv : r * v = v := by\n   101\t    have := VonNeumannAlgebra.star_mul_self_mul_eq_self (v := v) (by rw [hv2]; exact hridem)\n   102\t    rwa [hv2] at this\n   103\t  have hqv : q * v = v := by\n   104\t    calc q * v = q * (r * v) := by rw [hrv]\n   105\t      _ = (q * r) * v := by noncomm_ring\n   106\t      _ = r * v := by rw [hrq.2]\n   107\t      _ = v := hrv\n   108\t  refine ⟨⟨hv, hqv, hvq⟩, star_mem hv, ?_, ?_⟩\n   109\t  · have h := congrArg star hvq\n   110\t    rwa [star_mul, hqsa.star_eq] at h\n   111\t  · have h := congrArg star hqv\n   112\t    rwa [star_mul, hqsa.star_eq] at h\n   113\t\n   114\t/-- **`main.tex` Lemma `lem:finite_corner_finite_global` / `main.tex:1425-1451`.**\n   115\t\n   116\tIf the compressed vector functional `tau_q` is a faithful tracial state on the corner\n   117\t`q M q`, then `q` is a *finite projection of `M`*: it is not Murray–von Neumann\n   118\tequivalent to a proper subprojection of itself.\n   119\t\n   120\tThe manuscript argument is followed verbatim: from `v* v = q`, `v v* = r ≤ q` one gets\n   121\t`tau_q(r) = tau_q(v v*) = tau_q(v* v) = tau_q(q) = 1`, hence `tau_q(q - r) = 0`, and\n   122\tfaithfulness applied to the projection `q - r` gives `r = q`. -/\n   123\ttheorem isFiniteProjection_of_faithfulNormalTracialCorner {M : VonNeumannAlgebra H}\n   124\t    {q : H →L[ℂ] H} {Ω : H} (h : IsFaithfulNormalTracialCorner M q Ω) :\n   125\t    M.IsFiniteProjection q := by\n   126\t  have hqproj : M.IsProjection q := ⟨h.isStarProjection, h.mem⟩\n   127\t  have hqsa : IsSelfAdjoint q := h.isStarProjection.isSelfAdjoint\n   128\t  refine ⟨hqproj, ?_⟩\n   129\t  intro r hr hrq hequiv\n   130\t  obtain ⟨v, hv, hv1, hv2⟩ := hequiv\n   131\t  obtain ⟨hvcorner, hvstarcorner⟩ :=\n   132\t    mem_corner_of_mvNEquiv_projLe hqsa hqproj.mul_self hr.mul_self hv hv1 hv2 hrq\n   133\t  -- Traciality of `tau_q` on the corner gives `tau_q(r) = tau_q(q)`.\n   134\t  have htr : tauVec Ω (v * star v) = tauVec Ω (star v * v) :=\n   135\t    h.tracial_corner hvcorner hvstarcorner\n   136\t  rw [hv1, hv2] at htr\n   137\t  have hq1 : tauVec Ω q = 1 := h.apply_unit\n   138\t  have hr1 : tauVec Ω r = 1 := by rw [htr, hq1]\n   139\t  -- `q - r` is a projection of `M` living in the corner, with `tau_q(q - r) = 0`.\n   140\t  set x : H →L[ℂ] H := q - r with hxdef\n   141\t  have hx : M.IsProjection x := VonNeumannAlgebra.IsProjection.sub hr hqproj hrq\n   142\t  have hqx : q * x = x := by rw [hxdef, mul_sub, hqproj.mul_self, hrq.2]\n   143\t  have hxq : x * q = x := by rw [hxdef, sub_mul, hqproj.mul_self, hrq.1]\n   144\t  have hstarx : star x * x = x := by rw [hx.star_eq, hx.mul_self]\n   145\t  have hzero : cornerTau q Ω (star x * x) = 0 := by\n   146\t    rw [hstarx, cornerTau_apply, hqx, hxq]\n   147\t    have : ⟪Ω, x Ω⟫_ℂ = tauVec Ω x := rfl\n   148\t    rw [this, hxdef, map_sub, hq1, hr1, sub_self]\n   149\t  have hx0 : x = 0 := h.faithful x hx.2 hqx hxq hzero\n   150\t  have : q - r = 0 := hx0\n   151\t  exact (sub_eq_zero.mp this).symm\n   152\t\n   153\tend Finiteness\n   154\t\n   155\t/-! ## §2  Fullness of `q`\n   156\t\n   157\t`main.tex` Proposition `prop:fullness` (`main.tex:1475-1509`).  A central projection\n   158\t`z` of `M = A''` orthogonal to `q` kills `Ω`, hence kills the dense set of vectors\n   159\t`pi_omega(b) pi_omega(a) Ω`, hence vanishes.\n   160\t-/\n   161\t\n   162\tsection Fullness\n   163\t\n   164\t/-- **`main.tex` Proposition `prop:fullness`.**  Let `A` be a represented star algebra,\n   165\t`B` a set of operators commuting with `A`, and `Ω` a vector fixed by the projection `q`\n   166\tsuch that the vectors `b a Ω` (`a ∈ A`, `b ∈ B`) span a dense subspace.  Then `q` is a\n   167\t**full** projection of the von Neumann algebra `M = A''`: its central support is `1`.\n   168\t\n   169\tAuxiliary assumptions, both manuscript clauses: `hB` is `main.tex`\n   170\teq. `eq:M-commutes-complement` and `hdense` is `main.tex` eq. `eq:dense_states`. -/\n   171\ttheorem isFull_of_dense_cyclic_vectors {A : StarSubalgebra ℂ (H →L[ℂ] H)}\n   172\t    {B : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)} {q : H →L[ℂ] H} {Ω : H}\n   173\t    (hB : B ⊆ Set.centralizer (A : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)))\n   174\t    (hqΩ : q Ω = Ω)\n   175\t    (hdense : Dense (Submodule.span ℂ\n   176\t      {ξ : H | ∃ a ∈ (A : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)), ∃ b ∈ B, ξ = (b * a) Ω} : Set H)) :\n   177\t    (StarSubalgebra.vonNeumannGenerated A).IsFull q := by\n   178\t  set M : VonNeumannAlgebra H := StarSubalgebra.vonNeumannGenerated A with hMdef\n   179\t  refine VonNeumannAlgebra.isFull_of_forall_central ?_\n   180\t  intro z hz hz0 hzq\n   181\t  refine hz0 ?_\n   182\t  -- `z Ω = z q Ω = 0`.\n   183\t  have hzΩ : z Ω = 0 := by\n   184\t    have h1 : (z * q) Ω = (0 : H →L[ℂ] H) Ω := by rw [hzq]\n   185\t    rw [show (z * q) Ω = z (q Ω) from rfl, hqΩ] at h1\n   186\t    simpa using h1\n   187\t  have hzM : z ∈ M := VonNeumannAlgebra.mem_of_mem_center hz.2\n   188\t  have hvanish : ∀ ξ ∈ (Submodule.span ℂ\n   189\t      {ξ : H | ∃ a ∈ (A : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)), ∃ b ∈ B, ξ = (b * a) Ω}), z ξ = 0 := by\n   190\t    intro ξ hξ\n   191\t    induction hξ using Submodule.span_induction with\n   192\t    | mem ξ hξ =>\n   193\t        obtain ⟨a, ha, b, hb, rfl⟩ := hξ\n   194\t        have hbz : b * z = z * b :=\n   195\t          StarSubalgebra.mem_vonNeumannGenerated_iff.mp hzM b (hB hb)\n   196\t        have haM : a ∈ M := StarSubalgebra.mem_vonNeumannGenerated_of_mem ha\n   197\t        have haz : z * a = a * z := hz.commute haM\n   198\t        have hcomm : z * (b * a) = (b * a) * z := by\n   199\t          rw [← mul_assoc, ← hbz, mul_assoc, haz, ← mul_assoc]\n   200\t        have h1 : z ((b * a) Ω) = (z * (b * a)) Ω := rfl\n   201\t        rw [h1, hcomm, show ((b * a) * z) Ω = (b * a) (z Ω) from rfl, hzΩ, map_zero]\n   202\t    | zero => simp\n   203\t    | add ξ η _ _ hξ hη => rw [map_add, hξ, hη, add_zero]\n   204\t    | smul c ξ _ hξ => rw [map_smul, hξ, smul_zero]\n   205\t  have hfun : (z : H → H) = fun _ => 0 :=\n   206\t    Continuous.ext_on hdense z.continuous continuous_const fun ξ hξ => hvanish ξ hξ\n   207\t  exact ContinuousLinearMap.ext fun ξ => congrFun hfun ξ\n   208\t\n   209\tend Fullness\n   210\t\n   211\t/-! ## §3  Central summands, relative finiteness, and the type-III obstruction -/\n   212\t\n   213\tsection Summand\n   214\t\n   215\t/-- The **central summand** `z M` of a concrete von Neumann algebra, as a set of operators.\n   216\tIt is not a `VonNeumannAlgebra H` because its unit `z` is not `1`; the comparison theory\n   217\tbelow is therefore phrased relative to a set of operators. -/\n   218\tdef centralSummand (M : VonNeumannAlgebra H) (z : H →L[ℂ] H) : Set (H →L[ℂ] H) :=\n   219\t  (fun x => z * x) '' (M : Set (H →L[ℂ] H))\n   220\t\n   221\ttheorem mem_centralSummand_iff {M : VonNeumannAlgebra H} {z y : H →L[ℂ] H} :\n   222\t    y ∈ centralSummand M z ↔ ∃ x ∈ M, z * x = y := by\n   223\t  simp [centralSummand, eq_comm]\n   224\t\n   225\ttheorem mul_mem_centralSummand {M : VonNeumannAlgebra H} {z x : H →L[ℂ] H} (hx : x ∈ M) :\n   226\t    z * x ∈ centralSummand M z := ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩\n   227\t\n   228\ttheorem centralSummand_subset {M : VonNeumannAlgebra H} {z : H →L[ℂ] H}\n   229\t    (hz : M.IsCentralProjection z) : centralSummand M z ⊆ (M : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)) := by\n   230\t  rintro _ ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩\n   231\t  exact mul_mem (VonNeumannAlgebra.mem_of_mem_center hz.2) hx\n   232\t\n   233\t/-- Murray–von Neumann equivalence **relative to a set** `S` of operators: the implementing\n   234\tpartial isometry is required to lie in `S`. -/\n   235\tdef MvNEquivIn (S : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)) (p r : H →L[ℂ] H) : Prop :=\n   236\t  ∃ v ∈ S, star v * v = p ∧ v * star v = r\n   237\t\n   238\t/-- A projection is **finite relative to a set** `S` of operators when it is not equivalent,\n   239\tby a partial isometry of `S`, to a proper subprojection of itself belonging to `S`. -/\n   240\tdef IsFiniteProjectionIn (S : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)) (p : H →L[ℂ] H) : Prop :=\n   241\t  IsStarProjection p ∧ p ∈ S ∧\n   242\t    ∀ r, IsStarProjection r → r ∈ S → VonNeumannAlgebra.ProjLe r p →\n   243\t      MvNEquivIn S p r → r = p\n   244\t\n   245\t/-- The **type-III obstruction predicate**: a set of operators is *type-III-like* when it\n   246\tcontains no nonzero finite projection.  (For a von Neumann algebra this is precisely the\n   247\tdefining property of type III.)  The Lane-G conclusion is that no nonzero central summand\n   248\tof `M_Γ` has this property. -/\n   249\tdef IsTypeIIILike (S : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)) : Prop :=\n   250\t  ∀ p, IsStarProjection p → p ∈ S → p ≠ 0 → ¬ IsFiniteProjectionIn S p\n   251\t\n   252\t/-- Finiteness with respect to a larger algebra implies finiteness with respect to a smaller\n   253\tset of operators: there are fewer partial isometries available.  This is the manuscript's\n   254\tfinal step, \"`zq` is finite with respect to `z M_Γ`\". -/\n   255\ttheorem isFiniteProjectionIn_of_isFiniteProjection {M : VonNeumannAlgebra H}\n   256\t    {S : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)} {p : H →L[ℂ] H} (hSM : S ⊆ (M : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)))\n   257\t    (hp : M.IsFiniteProjection p) (hpS : p ∈ S) : IsFiniteProjectionIn S p := by\n   258\t  refine ⟨hp.1.1, hpS, fun r hr hrS hrp hequiv => ?_⟩\n   259\t  obtain ⟨v, hvS, hv1, hv2⟩ := hequiv\n   260\t  exact hp.2 r ⟨hr, hSM hrS⟩ hrp ⟨v, hSM hvS, hv1, hv2⟩\n   261\t\n   262\t/-- A nonzero finite projection in `S` refutes type-III-likeness of `S`. -/\n   263\ttheorem not_isTypeIIILike_of_isFiniteProjectionIn {S : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)} {p : H →L[ℂ] H}\n   264\t    (hp : IsFiniteProjectionIn S p) (hp0 : p ≠ 0) : ¬ IsTypeIIILike S :=\n   265\t  fun hS => hS p hp.1 hp.2.1 hp0 hp\n   266\t\n   267\tend Summand\n   268\t\n   269\t/-! ## §4  The main theorem: a nonzero finite projection in every nonzero central summand\n   270\t\n   271\t`main.tex` Theorem `thm:finite_projections_exist` (`main.tex:1511-1536`).\n   272\t-/\n   273\t\n   274\tsection Main\n   275\t\n   276\t/-- **`main.tex` Theorem `thm:finite_projections_exist`** — *the theorem whose conclusion\n   277\tcontains the nonzero finite projection* `z * q`.\n   278\t\n   279\tLet `M` be a concrete von Neumann algebra carrying the P50 faithful normal tracial corner\n   280\tstate `tau_q` at a projection `q`, and assume `q` is full (Proposition `prop:fullness`,\n   281\tproved above as `isFull_of_dense_cyclic_vectors`).  Then for every nonzero central\n   282\tprojection `z` of `M`:\n   283\t\n   284\t1. `z * q ≠ 0` — by fullness;\n   285\t2. `z * q` is a projection of `M`, dominated by `z` and by `q`;\n   286\t3. `z * q` is a **finite projection of `M`**;\n   287\t4. `z * q` lies in the central summand `z M`; and\n   288\t5. `z * q` is **finite relative to the summand** `z M` itself. -/\n   289\ttheorem central_summand_nonzero_finite_projection {M : VonNeumannAlgebra H}\n   290\t    {q : H →L[ℂ] H} {Ω : H} {z : H →L[ℂ] H}\n   291\t    (h : IsFaithfulNormalTracialCorner M q Ω) (hfull : M.IsFull q)\n   292\t    (hz : M.IsCentralProjection z) (hz0 : z ≠ 0) :\n   293\t    z * q ≠ 0 ∧ M.IsProjection (z * q) ∧\n   294\t      VonNeumannAlgebra.ProjLe (z * q) z ∧ VonNeumannAlgebra.ProjLe (z * q) q ∧\n   295\t      M.IsFiniteProjection (z * q) ∧ z * q ∈ centralSummand M z ∧\n   296\t      IsFiniteProjectionIn (centralSummand M z) (z * q) := by\n   297\t  have hqproj : M.IsProjection q := ⟨h.isStarProjection, h.mem⟩\n   298\t  have hqfin : M.IsFiniteProjection q := isFiniteProjection_of_faithfulNormalTracialCorner h\n   299\t  have hne : z * q ≠ 0 := hfull.mul_ne_zero hz hz0\n   300\t  have hzqproj : M.IsProjection (z * q) := hz.mul_isProjection hqproj\n   301\t  have hzqfin : M.IsFiniteProjection (z * q) := hqfin.mul_central hz\n   302\t  have hmem : z * q ∈ centralSummand M z := mul_mem_centralSummand hqproj.2\n   303\t  exact ⟨hne, hzqproj, hz.mul_projLe_left hqproj, hz.mul_projLe_right hqproj, hzqfin, hmem,\n   304\t    isFiniteProjectionIn_of_isFiniteProjection (centralSummand_subset hz) hzqfin hmem⟩\n   305\t\n   306\t/-- **Type-III exclusion.**  No nonzero central summand of `M` is type-III-like: it always\n   307\tcontains the nonzero finite projection `z * q`. -/\n   308\ttheorem not_isTypeIIILike_centralSummand {M : VonNeumannAlgebra H}\n   309\t    {q : H →L[ℂ] H} {Ω : H} {z : H →L[ℂ] H}\n   310\t    (h : IsFaithfulNormalTracialCorner M q Ω) (hfull : M.IsFull q)\n   311\t    (hz : M.IsCentralProjection z) (hz0 : z ≠ 0) :\n   312\t    ¬ IsTypeIIILike (centralSummand M z) := by\n   313\t  obtain ⟨hne, -, -, -, -, -, hfin⟩ :=\n   314\t    central_summand_nonzero_finite_projection h hfull hz hz0\n   315\t  exact not_isTypeIIILike_of_isFiniteProjectionIn hfin hne\n   316\t\n   317\tend Main\n   318\t\n   319\t/-! ## §5  Exported P51 theorem from the P50 input data -/\n   320\t\n   321\tsection Export\n   322\t\n   323\tvariable {ι : ℕ → Type*} [∀ n, Fintype (ι n)] [∀ n, DecidableEq (ι n)]\n   324\t\n   325\t/-- **Exported P51 theorem** (`main.tex:1456-1536`).\n   326\t\n   327\tThe input data are exactly those of the exported P50 theorem\n   328\t`NormalFaithfulCornerTrace.normal_faithful_corner_trace`: the compatible finite-codespace\n   329\tsystem `D` with GNS vector `Ω`, its decreasing projection tower, the represented regional\n   330\tC⋆-algebra `A` with its norm-density data, the commuting complementary set `B`, and the\n   331\tdense-vector premise.\n   332\t\n   333\tThe conclusion collects the three manuscript statements for `M = A''` and `q` the strong\n   334\tlimit of the stage projections:\n   335\t\n   336\t* `q` is a **finite** projection of `M` (Lemma `lem:finite_corner_finite_global`);\n   337\t* `q` is **full** in `M` (Proposition `prop:fullness`); and\n   338\t* every nonzero central projection `z` yields the **nonzero finite projection `z q` inside\n   339\t  the central summand `z M`**, so that summand is not type III\n   340\t  (Theorem `thm:finite_projections_exist`).\n   341\t\n   342\tNo global trace or weight on `M` is asserted, no direct integral is used, and the center of\n   343\t`M` is not claimed to be trivial. -/\n   344\ttheorem full_finite_corner_central_exclusion {Ω : H}\n   345\t    (D : CompatibleFiniteCodespaceSystem Ω ι)\n   346\t    (hp : IsDecreasingProjTower D.toFiniteCodespaceSystem.stageProj)\n   347\t    (A : StarSubalgebra ℂ (H →L[ℂ] H)) (hAclosed : IsClosed (A : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)))\n   348\t    (hlocal : ∀ n, Set.range (D.pi n) ⊆ (A : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)))\n   349\t    (hAdense : (A : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)) ⊆ closure (⋃ n, Set.range (D.pi n)))\n   350\t    (B : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)) (hB : B ⊆ Set.centralizer (A : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)))\n   351\t    (hdense : Dense (Submodule.span ℂ\n   352\t      {ξ : H | ∃ a ∈ (A : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)), ∃ b ∈ B, ξ = (b * a) Ω} : Set H)) :\n   353\t    (StarSubalgebra.vonNeumannGenerated A).IsFiniteProjection\n   354\t        (limitProj D.toFiniteCodespaceSystem.stageProj) ∧\n   355\t      (StarSubalgebra.vonNeumannGenerated A).IsFull\n   356\t        (limitProj D.toFiniteCodespaceSystem.stageProj) ∧\n   357\t      ∀ z, (StarSubalgebra.vonNeumannGenerated A).IsCentralProjection z → z ≠ 0 →\n   358\t        z * limitProj D.toFiniteCodespaceSystem.stageProj ≠ 0 ∧\n   359\t        IsFiniteProjectionIn\n   360\t          (centralSummand (StarSubalgebra.vonNeumannGenerated A) z)\n   361\t          (z * limitProj D.toFiniteCodespaceSystem.stageProj) ∧\n   362\t        ¬ IsTypeIIILike (centralSummand (StarSubalgebra.vonNeumannGenerated A) z) := by\n   363\t  set q := limitProj D.toFiniteCodespaceSystem.stageProj with hqdef\n   364\t  have hcorner :\n   365\t      IsFaithfulNormalTracialCorner (StarSubalgebra.vonNeumannGenerated A) q Ω :=\n   366\t    normal_faithful_corner_trace D hp A hAclosed hlocal hAdense B hB hdense\n   367\t  have hqΩ : q Ω = Ω :=\n   368\t    limitProj_apply_self fun n => D.toFiniteCodespaceSystem.stageProj_apply_self n\n   369\t  have hfull : (StarSubalgebra.vonNeumannGenerated A).IsFull q :=\n   370\t    isFull_of_dense_cyclic_vectors hB hqΩ hdense\n   371\t  refine ⟨isFiniteProjection_of_faithfulNormalTracialCorner hcorner, hfull, fun z hz hz0 => ?_⟩\n   372\t  obtain ⟨hne, -, -, -, -, -, hfin⟩ :=\n   373\t    central_summand_nonzero_finite_projection hcorner hfull hz hz0\n   374\t  exact ⟨hne, hfin, not_isTypeIIILike_of_isFiniteProjectionIn hfin hne⟩\n   375\t\n   376\tend Export\n   377\t\n   378\t/-! ## §6  Non-vacuity of the exported hypotheses\n   379\t\n   380\tThe exported theorem inherits the P50 premises and adds none beyond them.  The following\n   381\twitness re-instantiates them in the one-dimensional sanity system of P49/P50, showing that\n   382\tthe hypotheses of `full_finite_corner_central_exclusion` are simultaneously satisfiable.  It\n   383\tis a consistency check only and carries no manuscript content. -/\n   384\t\n   385\tsection Sanity\n   386\t\n   387\t/-- **Non-vacuity.**  Every hypothesis of the exported P51 theorem is satisfied by the\n   388\tone-dimensional sanity system, with `A = ⊤`, complementary algebra `{1}`, and GNS vector\n   389\t`EuclideanSpace.single 0 1`. -/\n   390\ttheorem sanity_full_finite_corner_central_exclusion :\n M aristotle_tasks/P49-finite-corner-trace.md\n M aristotle_tasks/P50-normal-faithful-corner-trace.md\n?? AristotleCandidates/FiniteCornerTrace.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/KaplanskyDensity.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/LocalHyperbolicAlgebraicAlpha.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/MixedUHFHyperfiniteFactor.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/NormalFaithfulCornerTrace.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/StrongOperatorClosedVonNeumann.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/VonNeumannBicommutantTheorem.lean\n?? reviews/P49-finite-corner-trace-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P49-finite-corner-trace-recovery.md\n?? reviews/P49A-strong-operator-closed-von-neumann-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P49B-von-neumann-bicommutant-theorem-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P49C-kaplansky-density-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P50-normal-faithful-corner-trace-closeout-rerun.md\n?? reviews/P50-normal-faithful-corner-trace-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P50-normal-faithful-corner-trace-recovery.md\n?? reviews/P53-local-hyperbolic-alg